niversity-wide', '["ALL"]', '["ALL"]', '["Dentistry (faculty-level agreement required; Danish only)","Medicine (limited clinical capacity; specific bilateral placement required)"]', NULL, '["English","Danish"]', 'substantial', 'Expected English proficiency comparable to TOEFL iBT 83 or IELTS 6.5 (no RHET 1020 exemption stated). Documentation varies by faculty: Aarhus BSS (none required); Health (none required); Arts (required for English degree programme only); Natural Sciences and Technical Sciences (documentation may be required).', 'None required for English-taught exchange courses (Danish required only for Danish-taught courses such as Dentistry; optional Danish language courses offered).', '["Spring","Academic Year","Summer"]', 'Autumn semester (AY 2026-2027): Mandatory AU Intro Days late-August/early-September; Courses late-August to late-January; Exam period mid-December to late-January (exact dates vary by study programme).', 'Spring semester (AY 2026-2027): Mandatory AU Intro Days late-January/early-February; Courses late-January to late-June; Exam period mid-May to late-June (exact dates vary by study programme).', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'EUR', 1000, 1000, 5526.0, 'partial', 'No mandatory host tuition or student union fee stated for exchange students. Stays >3 months are covered by Danish Health Insurance once issued a CPR number; stays <3 months require private health insurance. Students must arrange private travel, personal belongings, accident, and third-party liability insurance.', 'assisted', 'Optional AU Housing application is integrated into the admission application (deadlines Apr 1 Autumn / Oct 1 Spring). No housing guarantee; offers sent by Jul 1 (Autumn) and Dec 15 (Spring) with a 48-hour acceptance window requiring credit/debit card payment of 600 DKK non-refundable booking fee + first month''s rent (deposit of 1-3 months'' rent billed with 2nd month''s rent). Estimated AU Housing rent 350-600 EUR/mo (~3,000-4,000 DKK/mo); AU advises applying to Student Housing Aarhus (Ungdomsbolig Aarhus) as backup.', NULL, NULL, 'Non-EU/EEA students staying >3 months require a Danish student residence permit via SIRI. Normal processing takes up to 2 months (~60 days; up to 3 months if additional documentation is needed). Financial proof required: monthly funds matching the Danish SU grant benchmark (DKK 7,086/month at 2025 level, covering the full stay) in the student''s own bank account.', 'http://www.au.dk/en/', 'https://international.au.dk/education/admissions/exchange', 'https://kursuskatalog.au.dk/en/', NULL, 'ECTS; full-time study workload is 30 ECTS per semester (Danish grading scale: 12, 10, 7, 4, 02 passing; 00, -03 fail; some pass/fail exams).', 'Students must select courses from 1 faculty only (and most faculties allow 1 department only, per Brev.pdf#page=3). Law offers no Bachelor-level English courses (Master-level Law requires >=100 ECTS); Dentistry is Danish-only via faculty agreements; Medicine international semester has limited clinical capacity and requires Bachelor/3 years Medicine, C1 English, and clinical experience.', '["Online application via AU portal (post-nomination)","Official university transcript of records (PDF in English)","Bachelor''s degree diploma & transcript (if already earned and applying for Master-level courses)","Documentation of English language skills (faculty/department-dependent; not required for Aarhus BSS or Health)","Passport number (entered in the online application form)"]', 'Informal classroom culture with flat hierarchy (first-name basis with faculty), open critical discussion, and independent study; some courses enforce mandatory attendance for exam eligibility.', 'mid_size_city', 'multi_campus', 'high', 'Mandatory AU Intro Days (orientation before semester start with CPR/residence guidance, campus tours, social events), mentor/buddy contact via email where applicable, AU International Student Guide app, and Danish language courses.', 'Autumn semester (AY 2026-2027): Nomination 15 Feb - 25 Mar, Application 1 Mar - 1 Apr. Spring semester (AY 2026-2027): Nomination 15 Aug - 25 Sep, Application 1 Sep - 1 Oct (housing application deadline is the same).', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://international.au.dk/life/lifeindenmark/learningteachingcultures","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Informal classroom culture with flat hierarchy (first-name basis with faculty), open critical discussion, and independent study; some courses enforce mandatory attendance for exam eligibility."},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:2","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"University-wide"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:2","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:2","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG","GR"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"AY/Spring, Summer","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:2","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Spring","Academic Year","Summer"]},"campus_type":{"notes":"Aarhus University operates nationwide campuses in Aarhus (main campus), Emdrup (Copenhagen), Herning, Viborg, Roskilde, and Flakkebjerg.","source_ref":"https://international.au.dk/lifeinterm/yournewcity/aulocations","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"multi_campus"},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:2","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Aarhus"},"city_tier":{"notes":"Aarhus is Denmark''s second-largest city (>370,000 inhabitants per international.au.dk), mapped to mid_size_city.","source_ref":"https://international.au.dk/aboutau/profile/aarhus-and-surroundings","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":"mid_size_city"},"country":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:2","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Denmark"},"course_catalog_url":{"notes":"Official Aarhus University English course catalogue portal.","source_ref":"https://kursuskatalog.au.dk/en/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"https://kursuskatalog.au.dk/en/"},"course_restrictions_note":{"notes":"1-faculty/1-department rule corroborated in Brev.pdf#page=3; Law/Dentistry/Medicine subject rules come from AU official web course-information-restrictions.","source_ref":"https://international.au.dk/education/admissions/exchange/admission-to-aarhus-university/course-information-restrictions","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Students must select courses from 1 faculty only (and most faculties allow 1 department only, per Brev.pdf#page=3). Law offers no Bachelor-level English courses (Master-level Law requires >=100 ECTS); Dentistry is Danish-only via faculty agreements; Medicine international semester has limited clinical capacity and requires Bachelor/3 years Medicine, C1 English, and clinical experience."},"credit_system_and_load":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"ECTS; full-time study workload is 30 ECTS per semester (Danish grading scale: 12, 10, 7, 4, 02 passing; 00, -03 fail; some pass/fail exams)."},"cross_references":[],"daily_life_english_friendliness":{"notes":"au.dk explicitly notes Denmark ranks among the highest countries globally in English proficiency and accommodates English speakers in daily life and university services.","source_ref":"https://international.au.dk/about-au/profile/international-staff-and-researchers/life-in-denmark","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"high"},"eligible_auc_schools":{"notes":"Normalized from agreement_scope_raw == ''University-wide'' (faculty/subject exclusions documented in excluded_majors and course_restrictions_note).","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:2","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["ALL"]},"eligible_majors":{"notes":"Normalized from agreement_scope_raw == ''University-wide'' (subject-level exclusions noted in excluded_majors).","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:2","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["ALL"]},"english_course_availability":{"notes":"AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet p.3 states ''A wide variety of courses are taught in English. However, the selection of courses varies from semester to semester.''","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"substantial"},"english_course_list_url":{"notes":"No separate static English-only course list URL; filter Teaching language = English and Course type = Exchange at https://kursuskatalog.au.dk/en/.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"english_proficiency_and_rhet1020":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Expected English proficiency comparable to TOEFL iBT 83 or IELTS 6.5 (no RHET 1020 exemption stated). Documentation varies by faculty: Aarhus BSS (none required); Health (none required); Arts (required for English degree programme only); Natural Sciences and Technical Sciences (documentation may be required)."},"est_monthly_living_local":{"notes":"AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet p.4 publishes ''Monthly estimate 1.000'' EUR (itemized breakdown sums to 805-1,055 EUR: Housing 350-600 EUR, Meals 300 EUR, Books 25 EUR, Local transportation 30 EUR, Personal expenses incl. insurance 100 EUR). Official web also notes AU Housing ~3,000-4,000 DKK/mo and SIRI visa financial threshold DKK 7,086/mo.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":{"currency":"EUR","max":1000,"min":1000}},"excel_rows":[2],"exchange_page_url":{"notes":"Official incoming exchange URL embedded as hyperlink in AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet p.4.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"https://international.au.dk/education/admissions/exchange"},"excluded_majors":{"notes":"Dentistry (Danish-only) and Medicine (limited clinical capacity) exclusions documented on AU Course Information & Restrictions page; AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet (Brev.pdf#page=3) separately states the 1-faculty/1-department rule.","source_ref":"https://international.au.dk/education/admissions/exchange/admission-to-aarhus-university/course-information-restrictions","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":["Dentistry (faculty-level agreement required; Danish only)","Medicine (limited clinical capacity; specific bilateral placement required)"]},"ext":{},"fact_sheet_status":{"drive_links":["https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1J29DWUv_CmjK1xaPC6q7oQLy2khntHOi?usp=drive_link","https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1J29DWUv_CmjK1xaPC6q7oQLy2khntHOi"],"extracted_files":["data/raw/extracted/Aarhus University/2021-2022/Aarhus University Fact Sheet 2021-2022.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/Aarhus University/2022-23/Aarhus University Fact Sheet 2022-23.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/Aarhus University/2024-2025/Aarhus_University_Fact_Sheet_2024-25.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/Aarhus University/2025-2026/Aarhus_University_Fact_Sheet_2025-26_med_links.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf.txt"],"local_fil