.dk/life/locations/housing/auhousing/exchange-student/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"assisted"},"housing_notes":{"notes":"Timing and 350-600 EUR estimate also corroborated in Brev.pdf#page=2 and #page=4.","source_ref":"https://international.au.dk/life/locations/housing/auhousing/exchange-student/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Optional AU Housing application is integrated into the admission application (deadlines Apr 1 Autumn / Oct 1 Spring). No housing guarantee; offers sent by Jul 1 (Autumn) and Dec 15 (Spring) with a 48-hour acceptance window requiring credit/debit card payment of 600 DKK non-refundable booking fee + first month''s rent (deposit of 1-3 months'' rent billed with 2nd month''s rent). Estimated AU Housing rent 350-600 EUR/mo (~3,000-4,000 DKK/mo); AU advises applying to Student Housing Aarhus (Ungdomsbolig Aarhus) as backup."},"instruction_languages":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["English","Danish"]},"international_support_services":{"notes":"Further student arrival and mentor/language details on Brev.pdf#page=4.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Mandatory AU Intro Days (orientation before semester start with CPR/residence guidance, campus tours, social events), mentor/buddy contact via email where applicable, AU International Student Guide app, and Danish language courses."},"living_cost_usd_est":{"notes":"Converted from AU AY 2026-2027 official monthly estimate of 1,000 EUR over 5 months: 1000 EUR * 5 * FX rate 1.1052 USD/EUR = 5,526.00 USD. FX rate 1 EUR = 1.1052 USD (and 1 EUR = 7.4756 DKK; 1 DKK = 0.147841 USD) from ECB Euro reference exchange rates for 2026-11-13 (latest prior to 2026-11-15), retrieved 2026-11-15 at https://www.ecb.europa.eu/stats/policy_and_exchange_rates/euro_reference_exchange_rates/html/index.en.html.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":5526.0},"mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"No mandatory host tuition or student union fee stated for exchange students. Stays >3 months are covered by Danish Health Insurance once issued a CPR number; stays <3 months require private health insurance. Students must arrange private travel, personal belongings, accident, and third-party liability insurance."},"min_gpa_host":{"notes":"No centralized university-wide minimum GPA published in AY 2026-2027 fact sheet or AU incoming exchange pages.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"min_standing_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://international.au.dk/education/admissions/exchange/admission-to-aarhus-university/course-information-restrictions","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Bachelor-level courses are open to 2nd- and 3rd-year students (typically >=30 ECTS in field); Master-level courses are reserved for Master''s students (>=60 ECTS in field; Law Master''s >=100 ECTS)."},"nomination_deadlines":{"notes":"Also listed in nomination summary table on Brev.pdf#page=1.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Aarhus University/2026-2027/Brev.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Autumn semester (AY 2026-2027): Nomination 15 Feb - 25 Mar, Application 1 Mar - 1 Apr. Spring semester (AY 2026-2027): Nomination 15 Aug - 25 Sep, Application 1 Sep - 1 Oct (housing application deadline is the same)."},"official_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:2","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Aarhus University"},"official_website_url":{"notes":n