te July (AY 2020-2021 reference: Arrival Apr 1, Orientation Apr 2-7, Classes Apr 9 - Jul 29, Finals Jul 23-29; Winter program Jan-Mar open to Fall attendees).', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'JPY', 39934, 74272, 1784.49, 'partial', 'General deposit 20,000 JPY (partly refundable), International student activity fee 20,000 JPY/semester (non-refundable), initial 2-week meal plan 14,670 JPY (2020-21 PDF p.3); mandatory Japanese National Health Insurance plus Gakkensai/Inbound Futai-Gakuso insurance per aiu.ac.jp/en/st/financial/.', 'guaranteed', 'Komachi Hall 90,000 JPY/sem, Global Village 108,000-112,000 JPY/sem, University Village 108,000-114,000 JPY/sem, Sakura Village 180,000-184,000 JPY/sem + 20,000 JPY bedding/cleaning fee in 2020-21 PDF p.3; newer rates ~130,000-215,000+ JPY/sem on aiu.ac.jp/en/campuslife/housing/.', NULL, NULL, 'Requires Japanese Certificate of Eligibility (CoE) and Student Visa processed after AIU application.', 'http://www.aiu.ac.jp/', 'https://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/st/eligibility/', 'http://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/academic/', NULL, 'US-style semester credits (1 lecture cr = 15 class hrs; 50-min hours). Minimum 12 credits (required by Japanese immigration law), standard 15 credits (~5 x 3-credit courses), maximum 18 credits/semester.', 'Preparatory English courses, Teacher''s License courses, and required non-content courses for degree-seeking students are closed to incoming exchange students.', '["Home Online Nomination Form","Completed signed Application Form with Confirmation Sheet","Official Academic Transcript","One International Student Reference Form","Proof of English Proficiency (if applicable)","Two ID Photos","Copy of Passport","Evidence of Financial Support (for visa CoE)"]', 'Small liberal arts seminar/discussion classes averaging 18 students per class (Faculty of International Liberal Arts); 1 class hr = 50 min with expectation of 2 hrs independent prep per class hr.', NULL, 'rural', NULL, 'Center for International Affairs inbound exchange team, free arrival shuttle pickup from Akita Airport/JR station, orientation week, and residential life support.', 'Fall semester: Nomination Feb 1 - Feb 20, Application Feb 1 - Apr 1; Spring semester: Nomination Sep 1 - Sep 20, Application Sep 1 - Nov 1.', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Small liberal arts seminar/discussion classes averaging 18 students per class (Faculty of International Liberal Arts); 1 class hr = 50 min with expectation of 2 hrs independent prep per class hr."},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:3","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"University-wide"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:3","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:3","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"Fall/Spring","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:3","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Fall","Spring"]},"campus_type":{"notes":"aiu.ac.jp explicitly describes Yuwa, Akita as having ''the welcoming, friendly community you''d expect in a rural setting'' surrounded by nature.","source_ref":"https://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/about/explore-japan/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"rural"},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:3","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Akita"},"city_tier":{"notes":"Located in Yuwa, Akita City; official city population tier figure not cited on aiu.ac.jp.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"country":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:3","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Japan"},"course_catalog_url":{"notes":"Updated exchange academics portal also at https://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/st/academic/.","source_ref":"http://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/academic/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"http://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/academic/"},"course_restrictions_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Preparatory English courses, Teacher''s License courses, and required non-content courses for degree-seeking students are closed to incoming exchange students."},"credit_system_and_load":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"US-style semester credits (1 lecture cr = 15 class hrs; 50-min hours). Minimum 12 credits (required by Japanese immigration law), standard 15 credits (~5 x 3-credit courses), maximum 18 credits/semester."},"cross_references":[],"daily_life_english_friendliness":{"notes":"On-campus instruction and residential community use English (PDF p.1), while off-campus rural Akita is Japanese-speaking; overall local daily-life level unverified.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"eligible_auc_schools":{"notes":"Exact University-wide agreement scope.","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:3","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["ALL"]},"eligible_majors":{"notes":"Exact University-wide agreement scope.","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:3","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["ALL"]},"english_course_availability":{"notes":"All subject-matter courses in the Faculty of International Liberal Arts are taught in English.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"full"},"english_course_list_url":{"notes":"All subject-matter courses listed via https://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/academic/ and https://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/st/academic/ are taught in English; schedules hosted in ATOMS portal.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"english_proficiency_and_rhet1020":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"TOEFL iBT 71 or IELTS 6.0 (or equivalent) for non-native English speakers."},"est_monthly_living_local":{"notes":"Derived monthly cost from AY 2020-2021 Fact Sheet p.3 exact printed semester items divided by 5 months: Min = Komachi Residence 90,000 + Bedding & Cleaning 20,000 + Initial 2-wk meal plan 14,670 + 10-meal plan 60,000 + Textbooks 15,000 = 199,670 JPY / 5 = 39,934 JPY/mo; Max = Sakura Village (Fall) 184,000 + Bedding & Cleaning 20,000 + Initial 2-wk meal plan 14,670 + 21-meal plan 102,690 + Textbooks 50,000 = 371,360 JPY / 5 = 74,272 JPY/mo (excludes refundable 20,000 JPY deposit and 20,000 JPY activity fee; newer aiu.ac.jp pages cite textbooks ~50,000-70,000 JPY and housing ~130,000-215,000+ JPY/semester).","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":{"currency":"JPY","max":74272,"min":39934}},"excel_rows":[3],"exchange_page_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/st/eligibility/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"https://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/st/eligibility/"},"excluded_majors":{"notes":"No academic majors excluded; only preparatory English courses, Teacher''s License courses, and required degree-seeking non-content courses are closed (PDF p.2).","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"ext":{},"fact_sheet_status":{"drive_links":["https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1p2mwNxpqw9ye76JjCdmDe7DMwl30MiBY?usp=drive_link","https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1p2mwNxpqw9ye76JjCdmDe7DMwl30MiBY"],"extracted_files":["data/raw/extracted/Akita/Akita International University.pdf.txt"],"local_files":["data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf"],"match_status":"matched","notes":null},"fall_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://web.aiu.ac.jp/en/academic/academic-calendar/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Fall 2026: Arrival Aug 25, Orientation Aug 25-31, Classes Sep 2 - Dec 23, 2026 (Finals Dec 17-23, 2026)."},"final_semester_allowed":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_grants_or_stipends":{"notes":"No AIU incoming exchange stipend verified in local PDF or official aiu.ac.jp results.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_language_requirement":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"None required; Japanese language courses offered from beginner to advanced levels (advanced Japan Studies electives may require Japanese)."},"housing_availability":{"notes":"All international students are required to live in guaranteed on-campus housing (Komachi Hall, Global Village, University Village, or Sakura Village); homestay unavailable.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"guaranteed"},"housing_notes":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Komachi Hall 90,000 JPY/sem, Global Village 108,000-112,000 JPY/sem, University Village 108,000-114,000 JPY/sem, Sakura Village 180,000-184,000 JPY/sem + 20,000 JPY bedding/cleaning fee in 2020-21 PDF p.3; newer rates ~130,000-215,000+ JPY/sem on aiu.ac.jp/en/campuslife/housing/."},"instruction_languages":{"notes":"English for all subject-matter courses; Japanese language and Teacher''s License courses excepted.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["English"]},"international_support_services":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Center for International Affairs inbound exchange team, free arrival shuttle pickup from Akita Airport/JR station, orientation week, and residential life support."},"living_cost_usd_est":{"notes":"5-month estimate derived from monthly JPY range 39,934-74,272 (midpoint 57,103.0)/month. ECB cross-rate 1 EUR = 1.1052 USD and 1 EUR = 176.83 JPY -> 1 JPY = 0.006250 USD (2026-11-13, retrieved 2026-11-15 at https://www.ecb.europa.eu/stats/policy_and_exchange_rates/euro_reference_exchange_rates/html/index.en.html); 5-month USD est = 57,103.0 JPY * 5 * 0.006250 = 1,784.49 USD.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":1784.49},"mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Akita/Akita International University.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":"General deposit 20,000 JPY (partly refundable), International student activity fee 20,000 JPY/semester (non-refundable), initial 2-week meal plan 14,670 JPY (2020-21 PDF p.3); mandatory Japanese National Health Insurance plus Gakkensai/Inbound Futai-Gakuso insurance per aiu.ac.jp/en/st/financial/."},"min_gpa_host":{"notes":"Minimum cumulative