ice, pre-session/semester Italian language courses, MIL Service housing desk, Student Safety Package, YesMilano onboarding links."},"living_cost_usd_est":{"notes":"5-month midpoint estimate from EUR 1,500-2,200/month (EUR 1,850/mo) converted at ECB 2026-11-13 rate 1 EUR = 1.1052 USD (collected 2026-11-15, https://www.ecb.europa.eu/stats/policy_and_exchange_rates/euro_reference_exchange_rates/html/index.en.html); math: 1,850 * 5 * 1.1052 = 10,223.10 USD (approx. USD 10,223).","source_ref":"https://international.unicatt.it/ucscinternational-milan-accommodation","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":10223},"mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance":{"notes":"Details from p.4 and p.6-7.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Catholic University of the Sacred Heart (Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore)/2025-2026/UCSC IIS Spring 2026_all partners MILAN campus.pdf#page=6","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Mandatory EUR 80 enrolment fee (includes Student Safety Package health/liability insurance); EUR 45 activity fee for International Curriculum courses; pre-session or semester Italian language course EUR 400 each (EUR 600 combo); non-EU students must obtain International Health Insurance."},"min_gpa_host":{"notes":"Good academic standing defined as minimum 2.75/4.0 GPA (or 70-74/100; 24/30 ECTS C/C+).","source_ref":"https://international.unicatt.it/ucscinternational-semester-programs-exchange-program-in-milan","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":2.75},"min_standing_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://international.unicatt.it/ucscinternational-semester-programs-exchange-program-in-milan","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Completion of a minimum of 2 semesters at the undergraduate level."},"nomination_deadlines":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Catholic University of the Sacred Heart (Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore)/2025-2026/UCSC IIS Spring 2026_all partners MILAN campus.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Fall: nomination Mar 15, application Apr 15; Spring: nomination Oct 15, application Nov 15."},"official_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:16","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Catholic University of Sacred Heart (Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore)"},"official_website_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:16","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"http://www.unicatt.it/"},"region":{"notes":"From normalized manifest country/region mapping","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:16","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Europe"},"required_application_docs":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"schema_version":"1.0.0","seat_quota":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"shard":3,"short_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Catholic University of the Sacred Heart (Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore)/2025-2026/UCSC IIS Spring 2026_all partners MILAN campus.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"UCSC"},"slug":"catholic-university-of-sacred-heart-universita-cattolica-del-sacro-cuore","spring_term_dates":{"notes":"Dates from p.3-4; Faculty of Economics runs on a trimester calendar.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Catholic University of the Sacred Heart (Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore)/2025-2026/UCSC IIS Spring 2026_all partners MILAN campus.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"AY 2025-2026 Spring: Classes start Feb 23, 2026 (Economics Trimester begins Jan 7, 2026); Exams Jun 1-Jul 25, 2026."},"state_or_province":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"tuition_model":{"notes":"Exchange students remain enrolled and pay tuition to home institution; UCSC tuition waived (fee-paying Study Abroad is a separate track).","source_ref":"https://international.unicatt.it/ucscinternational-semester-programs-exchange-program-in-milan","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"auc_exchange_waiver"},"visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Catholic University of the Sacred Heart (Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore)/2025-2026/UCSC IIS Spring 2026_all partners MILAN campus.pdf#page=8","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":"Non-EU students require an Italian Type D study visa via Universitaly, valid International Health Insurance, and post-arrival Codice Fiscale; exact lead time and financial proof thresholds vary by consulate."}}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO universities (slug, excel_rows_json, shard, fact_sheet_match_status, fact_sheet_files_json, cross_references_json, official_name, short_name, country, state_or_province, city, region, agreement_status, agreement_student_levels_json, min_standing_note, agreement_scope_raw, eligible_auc_schools_json, eligible_majors_json, excluded_majors_json, min_gpa_host, instruction_languages_json, english_course_availability, english_proficiency_and_rhet1020, host_language_requirement, available_terms_json, fall_term_dates, spring_term_dates, final_semester_allowed, seat_quota, tuition_model, est_monthly_living_currency, est_monthly_living_min, est_monthly_living_max, living_cost_usd_est, living_cost_usd_est_status, mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance, housing_availability, housing_notes, host_grants_or_stipends, citizenship_restrictions, visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof, official_website_url, exchange_page_url, course_catalog_url, english_course_list_url, credit_system_and_load, course_restrictions_note, required_application_docs_json, academic_style, city_tier, campus_type, daily_life_english_friendliness, international_support_services, nomination_deadlines, ext_json, metadata_json) VALUES ('central-european-university', '[17]', 4, 'matched', '["data/raw/factsheets/Central European University (CEU)/2025-2026/CEU Fact Sheet 2025_2026_Final.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/Central European University (CEU)/2026-2027/CEU Fact Sheet_2026-27.pdf"]', '[]', 'Central European University', 'CEU', 'Austria', NULL, 'Vienna', 'Europe', 'active', '["UG"]', 'Home nomination and competitive application review required; BA exchange students can only be nominated for Winter + Spring terms combined, not Spring-only.', 'Political science', '["HUSS"]', '["Political Science"]', NULL, NULL, '["English"]', 'full', 'CEFR B2–C1 English expected (C1 cited on 2025-2026 sheet); TOEFL/IELTS/Cambridge or home institution CEFR confirmation letter; native speakers and graduates of fully English-taught BA/MA programs are exempt.', 'None required (English is the working language; optional free German courses offered).', '["Fall","Spring"]', 'AY 2026-2027 Fall: Mandatory Orientation Week Aug 31 – Sep 5, 2026; Fall Term Sep – Dec 2026.', 'AY 2026-2027 Winter Term Jan – Mar 2027; Spring Term Apr – Jun 2027 (BA exchange students must take Winter + Spring combined).', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'EUR', 1000, 1000, 5526.0, 'partial', 'Austrian Student Union (ÖH) fee 26.20 EUR/semester (52.40 EUR/year); mandatory health insurance required (EHIC for EU/EEA or MA35-compliant Austrian insurance for non-EU/EEA).', 'off_campus_only', 'CEU does not operate dormitories; incoming students arrange private/student housing in Vienna via guidance at https://www.ceu.edu/student-life/arriving/accommodation/faq.', NULL, NULL, 'Non-EU/EEA stays over 90 days require Visa D (up to 6 months) or Student Residence Permit; Austrian financial proof thresholds: 533.85 EUR/month (under 24) or 966.65 EUR/month (24+), plus rent exceeding 299.95 EUR/month.', 'https://www.ceu.edu/', 'https://www.ceu.edu/academics/bachelors/exchange', 'https://ceu.studyguide.timeedit.net/studies?mainTab=studies', NULL, 'Dual US credit and ECTS system (1 US credit = 2 ECTS); grading scale A (3.67+) down to C+ (2.33 minimum pass), F (0).', 'Exchange students must take at least 50% of courses/ECTS in their host department; BA students cannot enroll for Spring term alone without Winter term.', '["Online non-degree application form","Official university transcripts","Proof of English proficiency (or CEFR letter)","Approved course selection"]', 'US-style liberal arts', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Mandatory Orientation Week, Student Life Office visa/residence assistance, Academic Support, Counseling, Career Services, Disability Rights Officer, and free German classes.', 'AY 2026-2027 Fall: Nomination Apr 15 / Application Apr 30; Winter & Spring: Nomination Oct 15 / Application Oct 30.', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"note