 pre-term orientation, group Residence Card (RC) application service, GLAM student buddy program, and Korean Language Center (https://korean.cau.ac.kr/english/index.php?mid=n00)."},"living_cost_usd_est":{"notes":"5 months * 1075 USD/month midpoint = 5375.00 USD (rate 1 USD = 1 USD; verified 2026-11-15). Prorated from CAU Spring 2026 Fact Sheet official 16-week (~4-month) semester budget of $4,300 USD ($1,300 dorm + $700 meals + $600 transport + $200 books + $1,500 personal) = $1,075 USD/month.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Chung-Ang University/2026-2027/CAU - Fact Sheet_Spring 2026.pdf#page=6","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":5375.0},"mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance":{"notes":"Optional intensive Korean language courses carry a 25% discount for exchange students.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Chung-Ang University/2026-2027/CAU - Fact Sheet_Spring 2026.pdf#page=5","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Mandatory South Korean National Health Insurance (NHIS) enrollment upon Residence Card issuance at ~USD 70/month; private home insurance does not exempt from NHIS."},"min_gpa_host":{"notes":"Fall 2025 Fact Sheet (#page=6, confirmed via cau.ac.kr) explicitly states ''CAU does not have strict GPA requirements. Students nominated by their home universities will be deemed qualified'', and Spring 2026 Fact Sheet (#page=6) drops the 4.0 conversion table and specifies only Minimum 2.0/4.5 (75/100) for the whole semester.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"min_standing_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Chung-Ang University/2026-2027/CAU - Fact Sheet_Spring 2026.pdf#page=6","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"CAU does not enforce a strict incoming minimum GPA (Fall 2025 Fact Sheet #page=6: ''CAU does not have strict GPA requirements. Students nominated by their home universities will be deemed qualified''); Spring 2026 Fact Sheet specifies maintaining Minimum 2.0/4.5 (75/100) for the whole semester."},"nomination_deadlines":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Chung-Ang University/2026-2027/CAU - Fact Sheet_Spring 2026.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Fall Term: Nomination April, Application May; Spring Term: Nomination October (prior year), Application November (prior year)."},"official_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:20","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Chung-Ang University"},"official_website_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:20","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"https://www.cau.ac.kr/"},"region":{"notes":"From normalized manifest country/region mapping","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:20","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"East Asia"},"required_application_docs":{"notes":"Detailed across #page=2-3.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Chung-Ang University/2026-2027/CAU - Fact Sheet_Spring 2026.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["Official academic transcript (couriered original with Apostille/Consular authentication/CHSI for non-OECD & Chinese nationals)","Passport copy (valid >=6 months past stay)","Bank balance certificate (> USD 6,000/sem issued within 30 days + sponsorship letter if applicable)","Digital ID photo (3.5 x 4.5 cm)"]},"schema_version":"1.0.0","seat_quota":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"shard":6,"short_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Chung-Ang University/2026-2027/CAU - Fact Sheet_Spring 2026.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"CAU"},"slug":"chung-ang-university","spring_term_dates":{"notes":"Orientation/check-in timing on #page=4.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Chung-Ang University/2026-2027/CAU - Fact Sheet_Spring 2026.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Mar 2 – Jun (16 weeks); dorm check-in and mandatory orientation in the last week of February."},"state_or_province":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"tuition_model":{"notes":"Official CAU site confirms Student Exchange Program participants from partner universities study tuition-waived (Visiting Students pay tuition).","source_ref":"https://oia.cau.ac.kr/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"auc_exchange_waiver"},"visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof":{"notes":"Detailed across #page=2-4.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Chung-Ang University/2026-2027/CAU - Fact Sheet_Spring 2026.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"D-2-6 Exchange Student Visa (single-entry prior to Residence Card); post-arrival RC processing takes 7–10 weeks. Financial proof of > USD 6,000 (1 semester) or > USD 12,000 (1 year) issued within 30 days required (add''l docs for Egypt & 25 other nationals)."}}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO universities (slug, excel_rows_json, shard, fact_sheet_match_status, fact_sheet_files_json, cross_references_json, official_name, short_name, country, state_or_province, city, region, agreement_status, agreement_student_levels_json, min_standing_note, agreement_scope_raw, eligible_auc_schools_json, eligible_majors_json, excluded_majors_json, min_gpa_host, instruction_languages_json, english_course_availability, english_proficiency_and_rhet1020, host_language_requirement, available_terms_json, fall_term_dates, spring_term_dates, final_semester_allowed, seat_quota, tuition_model, est_monthly_living_currency, est_monthly_living_min, est_monthly_living_max, living_cost_usd_est, living_cost_usd_est_status, mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance, housing_availability, housing_notes, host_grants_or_stipends, citizenship_restrictions, visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof, official_website_url, exchange_page_url, course_catalog_url, english_course_list_url, credit_system_and_load, course_restrictions_note, required_application_docs_json, academic_style, city_tier, campus_type, daily_life_english_friendliness, international_support_services, nomination_deadlines, ext_json, metadata_json) VALUES ('college-of-charleston', '[21]', 7, 'matched', '["data/raw/factsheets/College of Charleston/2026-2027/Charleston Partner Information Sheet 2026-2027.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/College of Charleston/2026-2027/Charleston Partner Information Sheet 2027.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/College of Charleston/2026-2027/College of Charleston Support.pdf"]', '[]', 'College of Charleston', 'CofC', 'United States', 'South Carolina', 'Charleston', 'North America', 'active', '["UG","GR"]', NULL, 'University-wide', '["ALL"]', '["ALL"]', NULL, NULL, '["English"]', 'full', 'TOEFL iBT 80, IELTS 6.5, Duolingo 105, OR certification from home university confirming equivalent proficiency; RHET 1020 not specifically named, though home-university certification option is explicitly accepted.', NULL, '["Fall","Spring"]', 'Fall 2026: Arrival Aug 12, Orientation Aug 14, 2026 (Classes Aug 17-Dec 8, 2026 per https://charleston.edu/registrar/calendar/index.php).', 'Spring 2027: Arrival Jan 6, Orientation Jan 8, Classes Jan 11-May 4, 2027.', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'unknown', 'Mandatory CofC LewerMark health insurance billed to student account: $600/semester in AY 2026-2027/2027 sheet (was $522 Fall 2025 / $490 Spring 2026; https://lewermark.com/school/cofc/).', 'assisted', 'Apply via https://charleston.edu/housing/ (deadlines: May 1 Fall, Nov 1 Spring). Estimated Room & Board: $7,259/semester (AY 2026-2027/2027 sheet; also lists $3,444 personal/transport and $780 books/supplies per semester).', NULL, NULL, 'J-1 visa via Form DS-2019 issued by Center for International Education (CIE) after post-admission upload of Certificate of Finances and supporting bank statements/proof of funding covering living expenses ($12,083/sem total estimated Room & Board, personal/transport, books, and $600 insurance in 2027 sheet).', 'https://international.cofc.edu/', 'https://charleston.edu/international/international-students/incoming-exchange-students.php', 'https://catalog.cofc.edu/index.php', 'https://catalog.cofc.edu/index.php', NULL, 'All undergraduate academic areas open except School of Business restrictions: HTMT 488 and all ACCT courses other than ACCT 203 and ACCT 204 are closed; ECON 400, FINC 400, FINC 418, and MGMT 408 are evaluated case-by-case.', '["Home university nomination (~1 month prior via Jotform)","Online application form","Official home university transcript","Proof of English proficiency (TOEFL/IELTS/DET or home university certification)","Passport picture/data page copy","Certificate of Finances + proof of funding (post-admission)"]', 'Public liberal arts and sciences university (>10,000 students, >100 areas of study) emphasizing small-to-medium undergraduate classes in historic downtown Charleston.', NULL, 'urban', NULL, 'Cougar Ambassador Buddy Program, free Charleston (CHS) airport pickup on arrival day, virtual and in-person orientation, International Club, and monthly coffee hours/grocery trips.', 'Fall 2026 application Mar 6, 2026 (Fall 2027/AY Mar 5, 2027); Spring 2027 application Oct 2, 2026; nominations due ~1 month prior.', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/College of Charleston/2026-2027/Charleston Partner Information Sheet 2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Public liberal arts and sciences university (>10,000 students, >100 areas of study) emphasizing small-to-medium undergraduate classes in historic downtown Charleston."},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:21","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"University-wide"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:21","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:21","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG","GR"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"Fall/Spring","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:21","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Fall","Spring"]},"campus_type":{"notes":"Fact sheet p. 1 explicitly states campus is ''located in the historic downtown'' of Charleston (~130,000 residents).","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/College of Charleston/2026-2027/Charleston Partner Information Sheet 2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"urban"},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:21","source_type":"