Emlyon Business School/GBBA outline courses AY 2025-2026.pptx"],"match_status":"matched","notes":"Excel Col H blank, but matching public folder found in Drive master folder"},"fall_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://em-lyon.com/en/incoming-students","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":"Early September to late December (exact semester dates vary by GBBA vs MiM)"},"final_semester_allowed":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_grants_or_stipends":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_language_requirement":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://em-lyon.com/en/incoming-students","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":"French not required for English-taught exchange tracks; B2 French recommended if selecting French-taught courses."},"housing_availability":{"notes":"No on-campus dormitories; emlyon assists incoming students via its dedicated Studapart platform, private student residences (e.g., Nomad Campus), and homestay/intergenerational partners.","source_ref":"https://masters.em-lyon.com/en/Exchange-Students/Life-emlyon-business-school/Accommodation","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"assisted"},"housing_notes":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://masters.em-lyon.com/en/Exchange-Students/Life-emlyon-business-school/Accommodation","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Off-campus/private residences supported via emlyon''s Studapart portal and partner residence networks in Lyon."},"instruction_languages":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://em-lyon.com/en/incoming-students","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":["English","French"]},"international_support_services":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://em-lyon.com/en/international/incoming-students/first-steps-france","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Incoming Students desk, Studapart housing portal, First Steps in France visa/Sécurité Sociale onboarding support."},"living_cost_usd_est":{"notes":"5-month estimate: 1,000 EUR/month * 5 months = 5,000 EUR * 1.1052 USD/EUR = 5,526.00 USD (ECB 2026-11-13 rate, collected 2026-11-15: https://www.ecb.europa.eu/stats/policy_and_exchange_rates/euro_reference_exchange_rates/html/index.en.html).","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Emlyon Business School/Factsheet_MiM_2025_-_2026_V.1_3_.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":5526.0},"mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance":{"notes":"CVEC exemption rules verified via official French student portal (etudiant.gouv.fr / campusfrance.org); ameli portal via https://etudiant-etranger.ameli.fr/#/.","source_ref":"https://em-lyon.com/en/international/incoming-students/first-steps-france","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Bilateral exchange students are EXEMPT from the French CVEC student life fee (obtain free exemption certificate at cvec.etudiant.gouv.fr per Campus France/etudiant.gouv.fr). Registration for French Sécurité Sociale (etudiant-etranger.ameli.fr) is mandatory for stays >3 months, plus third-party civil liability insurance (~EUR 10)."},"min_gpa_host":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"min_standing_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"nomination_deadlines":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://em-lyon.com/en/incoming-students","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Fall Semester: partner nomination May 1, student application May 15. Spring Semester: partner nomination October 1, student application October 10."},"official_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:34","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Emlyon Business School"},"official_website_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:34","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"http://www.em-lyon.com/"},"region":{"notes":"From normalized manifest country/region mapping","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:34","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Europe"},"required_application_docs":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"schema_version":"1.0.0","seat_quota":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"shard":8,"short_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://em-lyon.com/en/incoming-students","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"emlyon"},"slug":"emlyon-business-school","spring_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://em-lyon.com/en/incoming-students","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":"Early January/February to late April/May (exact semester dates vary by GBBA vs MiM)"},"state_or_province":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"tuition_model":{"notes":"Incoming academic exchange students under partner agreements pay tuition at their home institution and have emlyon tuition fees waived.","source_ref":"https://em-lyon.com/en/incoming-students","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"auc_exchange_waiver"},"visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof":{"notes":"Visa portals also listed at https://france-visas.gouv.fr/en/web/france-visas/visa-wizard and https://pastel.diplomatie.gouv.fr/etudesenfrance.","source_ref":"https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/eli/decret/2026/6/22/INTV2605727D/jo/texte","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Non-EU students staying >90 days must obtain a French VLS-TS long-stay student visa via Etudes en France (pastel.diplomatie.gouv.fr/etudesenfrance) / France-Visas before departure. Effective August 1, 2026, Décret n° 2026-526 increased minimum student financial proof from EUR 615/mo to EUR 877.50/month (EUR 10,530/year; 47% of gross SMIC)."}}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO universities (slug, excel_rows_json, shard, fact_sheet_match_status, fact_sheet_files_json, cross_references_json, official_name, short_name, country, state_or_province, city, region, agreement_status, agreement_student_levels_json, min_standing_note, agreement_scope_raw, eligible_auc_schools_json, eligible_majors_json, excluded_majors_json, min_gpa_host, instruction_languages_json, english_course_availability, english_proficiency_and_rhet1020, host_language_requirement, available_terms_json, fall_term_dates, spring_term_dates, final_semester_allowed, seat_quota, tuition_model, est_monthly_living_currency, est_monthly_living_min, est_monthly_living_max, living_cost_usd_est, living_cost_usd_est_status, mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance, housing_availability, housing_notes, host_grants_or_stipends, citizenship_restrictions, visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof, official_website_url, exchange_page_url, course_catalog_url, english_course_list_url, credit_system_and_load, course_restrictions_note, required_application_docs_json, academic_style, city_tier, campus_type, daily_life_english_friendliness, international_support_services, nomination_deadlines, ext_json, metadata_json) VALUES ('frankfurt-school-of-finance-and-management', '[35]', 1, 'matched', '["data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2020_2021/Frankfurt School of Finance _ Management.docx","data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2025_2026/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2025_26.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf"]', '[]', 'Frankfurt School of Finance & Management', 'Frankfurt School', 'Germany', NULL, 'Frankfurt', 'Europe', 'active', '["UG","GR"]', 'Bachelor exchange: at least 2 years completed in a business or economics-related programme (eligible for 6th/7th semester modules). Master exchange: completed undergraduate degree and at least 1 semester at graduate level.', 'Business Administration', '["BUS"]', '["Business Administration"]', NULL, NULL, '["English","German"]', 'substantial', 'TOEFL iBT 90, IELTS 7.0, or Cambridge C1 (within 2 years of test date), OR confirmation from home university study advisory office if degree programme at home university is fully taught in English (native speakers provide native-English passport proof). RHET 1020 is not specifically mentioned; AUC English-medium degree confirmation letter satisfies the home-programme English exemption.', 'C1 German proficiency required only if enrolling in German-taught modules; no German required for English-taught modules. Optional German courses offered (6 ECTS during semester; optional 1-month intensive August course before Winter semester for a fee).', '["Spring","Academic Year"]', 'AY 2026-2027 Winter semester (available under Academic Year option): Mandatory orientation 19–20 Aug 2026; Bachelor lectures 17 Aug–11 Dec 2026 (Exam I 17–24 Oct, Exam II 12–19 Dec 2026); Master term 1 Sep 2026–31 Jan 2027 (lectures begin 31 Aug, end 12 Dec; Exam I 19–24 Oct, Exam II 14–19 Dec 2026).', 'AY 2026-2027 Summer semester 2027: Mandatory orientation 21–22 Jan 2027; Bachelor lectures 25 Jan–21 May 2027 (Exam I 13–20 Mar, Exam II 22–29 May 2027); Master term 1 Feb–31 Aug 2027 (lectures begin 11 Jan, end 22 May; Exam I 15–20 Mar, Exam II 24–29 May 2027).', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'EUR', 900, 1200, 5802.3, 'partial', 'Mandatory reduced Deutschlandticket (~EUR 189/semester) and Student Council fee (EUR 15/semester) apply to all enrolled students regardless of length of stay. Compulsory German-equivalent unlimited health insurance covering the full semester (travel insurance rejected; checked at mandatory orientation, or students must enroll in German insurance at ~EUR 105/month).', 'assisted', 'Limited furnished on-campus apartments (private bath and kitchenette) reserved with dorm partner i-Live on a first-come, first-served basis (not guaranteed; apply within online exchange application). Fixed 6-month solidarity contracts (15 Jan–14 Jul or 15 Jul–14 Jan) at EUR 770/month (14-day withdrawal period, after which full 6-month rent applies; contracted directly with i-Live). Other Frankfurt options: http://www.frankfurt-school.de/en/home/about/campus/dorms', NULL, NULL, 'Compulsory pre-arrival German student visa for non-EU students (arranged individually via local German embassy; must be valid for mandatory pre-semester orientation days per AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=2). German Federal Foreign Office blocked-account financial standard is EUR 992/month (EUR 11,904/year) per https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/sperrkonto/388600.', 'http://www.frankfurt-school.de/content/en.html', 'https://www.frankfurt-school.de/en/students-alumni/international-office/incoming-students', NULL, NULL, 'ECTS credits (each FS module = 6 ECTS). Exchange workload: minimum 1 module (6 ECTS), maximum 5 modules (30 ECTS) per semester including optional 6-ECTS German course.', 'Bachelor exchange limited to 6th and 7th semester BA modules; most Master modules open subject to availability. Add/drop available before semester start; enrollment in specific courses not guaranteed. Lectures and exams run Monday–Saturday (#page=1); exam dates released ~1–2 weeks before exam week.', '["Proof of English and/or German proficiency","Official stamped and signed Transcript of Records","Bachelor degree certificate (Master exchange only)","Passport copy (valid for full semester)","Biometric passport-style photograph","Proof of international health insurance"]', 'Research-led, triple-accredited (AACSB, AMBA, EQUIS) business school focusing on finance, management, economics, accounting, and philosophy & law; lectures and exams run Monday–Saturday, with mandatory orientation and online course selection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Mandatory International Student Orientation (campus tour, FS Online Campus onboarding, compulsory health insurance check), optional semester German course (6 ECTS) and August intensive German course, dedicated Incoming Student Mobility Manager (Patricia Escalera, p.escalera@fs.de; #page=2), International Office walk-in hours Mon–Fri 9:00–16:00 and 24/7 campus reception (#page=3).', 'Summer Semester (Spring): Nomination 1 October / Application 1 November; Winter Semester (Fall / Academic Year): Nomination 15 April / Application 15 May.', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Research-led, triple-accredited (AACSB, AMBA, EQUIS) business school focusing on finance, management, economics, accounting, and philosophy & law; lectures and exams run Monday–Saturday, with mandatory orientation and online course selection."},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Business Administration"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG","GR"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"AY/Spring","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Spring","Academic Year"]},"campus_type":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":"No citizenship restrictions stated; non-EU nationals require a pre-arrival German student visa.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Frankfurt"},"city_tier":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"country":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Germany"},"course_catalog_url":{"notes":"AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=2 states the module catalogue is made available by the International Office prior to course selection periods (July/December for BA, July/November for MA), and course selection occurs via FS Online Campus.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"course_restrictions_note":{"notes":"Mon–Sat schedule and exam-release note on #page=1.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Bachelor exchange limited to 6th and 7th semester BA modules; most Master modules open subject to availability. Add/drop available before semester start; enrollment in specific courses not guaranteed. Lectures and exams run Monday–Saturday (#page=1); exam dates released ~1–2 weeks before exam week."},"credit_system_and_load":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"ECTS credits (each FS module = 6 ECTS). Exchange workload: minimum 1 module (6 ECTS), maximum 5 modules (30 ECTS) per semester including optional 6-ECTS German course."},"cross_references":[],"daily_life_english_friendliness":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"eligible_auc_schools":{"notes":"Mapped from Excel agreement_scope_raw ''Business Administration'' (AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=1 lists Finance, Management, Economics, Philosophy & Law, Accounting departments).","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"partial","value":["BUS"]},"eligible_majors":{"notes":"Excel agreement_scope_raw states ''Business Administration''; AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=1 offers modules in finance, economics, management, accounting, philosophy & law.","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Business Administration"]},"english_course_availability":{"notes":"AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=2: Master programmes are completely taught in English; most 6th/7th-semester Bachelor modules are taught in English.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"substantial"},"english_course_list_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"english_proficiency_and_rhet1020":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"TOEFL iBT 90, IELTS 7.0, or Cambridge C1 (within 2 years of test date), OR confirmation from home university study advisory office if degree programme at home university is fully taught in English (native speakers provide native-English passport proof). RHET 1020 is not specifically mentioned; AUC English-medium degree confirmation letter satisfies the home-programme English exemption."},"est_monthly_living_local":{"notes":"Official FS International Student Guide (''Before you Apply'') cites DAAD guidance of EUR 900–1,200/month covering accommodation, groceries, health insurance, transport, communication, study materials, and personal expenses (note AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=2 also lists optional i-Live dorm rent at EUR 770/month).","source_ref":"https://www.frankfurt-school.de/en/live/international-student-guide/before-you-apply","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":{"currency":"EUR","max":1200,"min":900}},"excel_rows":[35],"exchange_page_url":{"notes":"Embedded PDF /Annots link on p.1 and p.2 of AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet; FS website also hosts https://www.frankfurt-school.de/en/students/international-office/incoming","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"https://www.frankfurt-school.de/en/students-alumni/international-office/incoming-students"},"excluded_majors":{"notes":"No specific majors excluded; AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=2 limits Bachelor exchange students to 6th and 7th semester BA modules.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"ext":{},"fact_sheet_status":{"drive_links":["https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1hYkLDA896DBrzHduic16B6V6zD7WO3tW?usp=drive_link","https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1hYkLDA896DBrzHduic16B6V6zD7WO3tW"],"extracted_files":["data/raw/extracted/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2020_2021/Frankfurt School of Finance _ Management.docx.txt","data/raw/extracted/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2025_2026/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2025_26.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf.txt"],"local_files":["data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2020_2021/Frankfurt School of Finance _ Management.docx","data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2025_2026/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2025_26.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf"],"match_status":"matched","notes":null},"fall_term_dates":{"notes":"Excel agreement_terms_raw is ''AY/Spring''; Winter semester dates apply to Academic Year students.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"AY 2026-2027 Winter semester (available under Academic Year option): Mandatory orientation 19–20 Aug 2026; Bachelor lectures 17 Aug–11 Dec 2026 (Exam I 17–24 Oct, Exam II 12–19 Dec 2026); Master term 1 Sep 2026–31 Jan 2027 (lectures begin 31 Aug, end 12 Dec; Exam I 19–24 Oct, Exam II 14–19 Dec 2026)."},"final_semester_allowed":{"notes":"AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=2 does not forbid final-semester students, but strongly advises against relying on specific FS courses to meet graduation requirements because course enrollment is not guaranteed.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_grants_or_stipends":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_language_requirement":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"C1 German proficiency required only if enrolling in German-taught modules; no German required for English-taught modules. Optional German courses offered (6 ECTS during semester; optional 1-month intensive August course before Winter semester for a fee)."},"housing_availability":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"assisted"},"housing_notes":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Limited furnished on-campus apartments (private bath and kitchenette) reserved with dorm partner i-Live on a first-come, first-served basis (not guaranteed; apply within online exchange application). Fixed 6-month solidarity contracts (15 Jan–14 Jul or 15 Jul–14 Jan) at EUR 770/month (14-day withdrawal period, after which full 6-month rent applies; contracted directly with i-Live). Other Frankfurt options: http://www.frankfurt-school.de/en/home/about/campus/dorms"},"instruction_languages":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["English","German"]},"international_support_services":{"notes":"Also cites #page=2 for German courses/contact and #page=3 for office/reception hours.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Mandatory International Student Orientation (campus tour, FS Online Campus onboarding, compulsory health insurance check), optional semester German course (6 ECTS) and August intensive German course, dedicated Incoming Student Mobility Manager (Patricia Escalera, p.escalera@fs.de; #page=2), International Office walk-in hours Mon–Fri 9:00–16:00 and 24/7 campus reception (#page=3)."},"living_cost_usd_est":{"notes":"5-month USD midpoint estimate derived from EUR 900–1,200/month range (midpoint EUR 1,050/mo x 5 = EUR 5,250) converted at ECB 2026-11-13 reference rate 1 EUR = 1.1052 USD (collected 2026-11-15 via https://www.ecb.europa.eu/stats/policy_and_exchange_rates/euro_reference_exchange_rates/html/index.en.html): 5,250 x 1.1052 = 5,802.30 USD.","source_ref":"https://www.frankfurt-school.de/en/live/international-student-guide/before-you-apply","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":5802.3},"mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Mandatory reduced Deutschlandticket (~EUR 189/semester) and Student Council fee (EUR 15/semester) apply to all enrolled students regardless of length of stay. Compulsory German-equivalent unlimited health insurance covering the full semester (travel insurance rejected; checked at mandatory orientation, or students must enroll in German insurance at ~EUR 105/month)."},"min_gpa_host":{"notes":"No institutional minimum GPA stated in AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet; partner institutions handle nomination screening.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"min_standing_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Bachelor exchange: at least 2 years completed in a business or economics-related programme (eligible for 6th/7th semester modules). Master exchange: completed undergraduate degree and at least 1 semester at graduate level."},"nomination_deadlines":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Summer Semester (Spring): Nomination 1 October / Application 1 November; Winter Semester (Fall / Academic Year): Nomination 15 April / Application 15 May."},"official_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Frankfurt School of Finance & Management"},"official_website_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"http://www.frankfurt-school.de/content/en.html"},"region":{"notes":"From normalized manifest country/region mapping","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:35","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Europe"},"required_application_docs":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["Proof of English and/or German proficiency","Official stamped and signed Transcript of Records","Bachelor degree certificate (Master exchange only)","Passport copy (valid for full semester)","Biometric passport-style photograph","Proof of international health insurance"]},"schema_version":"1.0.0","seat_quota":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"shard":1,"short_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Frankfurt School"},"slug":"frankfurt-school-of-finance-and-management","spring_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"AY 2026-2027 Summer semester 2027: Mandatory orientation 21–22 Jan 2027; Bachelor lectures 25 Jan–21 May 2027 (Exam I 13–20 Mar, Exam II 22–29 May 2027); Master term 1 Feb–31 Aug 2027 (lectures begin 11 Jan, end 22 May; Exam I 15–20 Mar, Exam II 24–29 May 2027)."},"state_or_province":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"tuition_model":{"notes":"Standard FS tuition fees are waived for incoming exchange students nominated under partner exchange agreements; mandatory Deutschlandticket and Student Council fees still apply.","source_ref":"https://www.frankfurt-school.de/en/students/international-office/incoming","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"auc_exchange_waiver"},"visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Frankfurt School of Finance & Management/2026-2027/Fact_Sheet_Exchange_Students_2026_27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Compulsory pre-arrival German student visa for non-EU students (arranged individually via local German embassy; must be valid for mandatory pre-semester orientation days per AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=2). German Federal Foreign Office blocked-account financial standard is EUR 992/month (EUR 11,904/year) per https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/sperrkonto/388600."}}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO universities (slug, excel_rows_json, shard, fact_sheet_match_status, fact_sheet_files_json, cross_references_json, official_name, short_name, country, state_or_province, city, region, agreement_status, agreement_student_levels_json, min_standing_note, agreement_scope_raw, eligible_auc_schools_json, eligible_majors_json, excluded_majors_json, min_gpa_host, instruction_languages_json, english_course_availability, english_proficiency_and_rhet1020, host_language_requirement, available_terms_json, fall_term_dates, spring_term_dates, final_semester_allowed, seat_quota, tuition_model, est_monthly_living_currency, est_monthly_living_min, est_monthly_living_max, living_cost_usd_est, living_cost_usd_est_status, mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance, housing_availability, housing_notes, host_grants_or_stipends, citizenship_restrictions, visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof, official_website_url, exchange_page_url, course_catalog_url, english_course_list_url, credit_system_and_load, course_restrictions_note, required_application_docs_json, academic_style, city_tier, campus_type, daily_life_english_friendliness, international_support_services, nomination_deadlines, ext_json, metadata_json) VALUES ('freie-universitat-berlin', '[36,37]', 2, 'matched', '["data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/2024-2025/Courses/FUB English Courses Summer 2024.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/2024-2025/Courses/FUB English Courses Winter 2023-24.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/2024-2025/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2025-2026.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/FUB English Courses Summer 2025.xlsx","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/FUB English Courses Winter 2024-25.xlsx","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2022-2023.pdf"]', '[]', 'Freie Universität Berlin', 'FU Berlin', 'Germany', NULL, 'Berlin', 'Europe', 'active', '["UG","GR"]', 'Must be nominated by home university; in general BA students cannot enroll in Master''s programs or individual Master''s-level courses (case-by-case departmental exceptions possible); visiting PhD enrollment possible with prerequisites.', 'University-wide', '["ALL"]', '["ALL"]', '["Human Medicine","Veterinary Medicine","Fee-based continuing education master''s programs"]', NULL, '["German","English"]', 'limited', 'No general English test certificate stated for most departments; CEFR C1 English level required for courses at the John F. Kennedy Institute for North American Studies.', 'Exempt from DSH/TestDaF exam and no certificate required (home university verifies); expected German CEFR B2 for Humanities & Social Sciences and B1 for Natural Sciences. Optional pre-semester 6-week intensive German course (~900 EUR, all levels incl. beginners) and free in-semester German courses (placement test required).', '["Spring","Academic Year"]', 'Winter Term 2026/2027: Semester Oct 1, 2026 – Mar 31, 2027; Orientation first week of October; Lecture period Oct 12, 2026 – Feb 19, 2027; Exams typically during last two weeks of lecture period (varies by department).', 'Summer Term 2027: Semester Apr 1, 2027 – Sep 30, 2027; Orientation first week of April; Lecture period Apr 12, 2027 – Jul 23, 2027; Exams typically during last two weeks of lecture period (varies by department).', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'EUR', 934, 934, 5161.28, 'partial', 'Exempt from university tuition; mandatory semester ticket and social fees ~310 EUR/semester (paid prior to arrival). Mandatory comprehensive German health insurance required for enrollment and residence permit (~150 EUR/month for students under age 30 via German public student insurance; external waivers rarely accepted unless EHIC/GHIC or unlimited coverage).', 'assisted', 'No on-campus accommodation available (per AY 2025-2026 Fact Sheet #page=3). Students may arrange private housing (e.g., WG shared flats) or apply via FU Berlin''s ERG Accommodation Service (dorms, shared apartments, furnished single apartments; ~500-1,200 EUR/month). First-come, first-served; mandatory online registration deadlines June 10 (Winter term) and December 10 (Summer term).', NULL, NULL, 'Non-EU/EEA/non-exempt nationals (incl. Egypt) must obtain a German student visa prior to arrival (processing takes at least 8 weeks, up to several months, per Fact Sheet #page=2). After arrival, non-EU students apply for a Berlin residence permit (Aufenthaltserlaubnis) via LEA/FU Pass-Service (typically 8 to 14 weeks processing). Financial proof (e.g., blocked account / Sperrkonto) required per German Federal Foreign Office standard (992 EUR/month / 11,904 EUR/year; FU Berlin general FAQ lists >=934 EUR/month).', 'https://www.fu-berlin.de/en/', 'https://www.fu-berlin.de/en/studium/international/studium_fu/auslandssemester/direktaustausch_in/index.html', 'https://www.fu-berlin.de/vv/en/fb', NULL, 'ECTS (Leistungspunkte/LP); regular full-time workload is 30 ECTS per semester (FU recommends 10-30 ECTS for exchange students; no strict host minimum). Grading scale (except Law): 1.0-1.5 very good, 1.6-2.5 good, 2.6-3.5 satisfactory, 3.5-4.0 sufficient, 5.0 fail.', 'Human Medicine, Veterinary Medicine, and fee-based continuing education Master''s programs are closed. Biochemistry, bioinformatics, and biology depend on lab availability and prior departmental approval; restrictions apply in Pharmacy, Law (prefers reciprocal Law exchange partners), and Business & Economics (requires B2+ German; very limited irregular English offerings). Master''s courses other than Modern German Literature, Philosophy, and Political Science require prior departmental approval; BA students generally cannot take Master''s courses. Cross-registration at HU Berlin, TU Berlin, and University of Potsdam possible with prior lecturer approval.', '["Official home university nomination (email or letter)","Online MoveON application form","Passport photocopy (photo page)","University transcript of records (German or English)","Copies of completed B.A./M.A./other degrees (if available)","Proof of comprehensive German/valid health insurance & semester fee payment (for enrollment)"]', 'Modular structure (lecture + seminar pairings per module) at a German research university (University of Excellence / Berlin University Alliance) with cross-registration across HU Berlin, TU Berlin, and University of Potsdam.', 'metropolis', NULL, NULL, 'Mandatory orientation program (5-10 days before lectures: course selection, FU-Net/campus tours), Distributed Campus onboarding portal, Pass Service (arrival residence permit assistance), pre-semester and free in-semester German language courses via ZE Sprachenzentrum, plus dedicated Exchange courses in German culture/history/society.', 'Winter term: Nomination & student application deadline April 30; Summer term: Nomination & student application deadline October 30.', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Modular structure (lecture + seminar pairings per module) at a German research university (University of Excellence / Berlin University Alliance) with cross-registration across HU Berlin, TU Berlin, and University of Potsdam."},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"University-wide"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":"Excel Col D note: ''Exchange and erasmus''","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG","GR"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"AY/Spring","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Spring","Academic Year"]},"campus_type":{"notes":"Main Iltisstrasse 4 address in Dahlem noted on Fact Sheet p.1, while exact campus_type (multi_campus across Dahlem/Lankwitz/Düppel) was not directly cited from a saved fu-berlin.de URL.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Berlin"},"city_tier":{"notes":"AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet p.2 explicitly refers to the ''Berlin metropolitan area'' (German capital metropolis).","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"metropolis"},"country":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Germany"},"course_catalog_url":{"notes":"Official FU Berlin course catalog URL embedded in AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet p.3.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"https://www.fu-berlin.de/vv/en/fb"},"course_restrictions_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Human Medicine, Veterinary Medicine, and fee-based continuing education Master''s programs are closed. Biochemistry, bioinformatics, and biology depend on lab availability and prior departmental approval; restrictions apply in Pharmacy, Law (prefers reciprocal Law exchange partners), and Business & Economics (requires B2+ German; very limited irregular English offerings). Master''s courses other than Modern German Literature, Philosophy, and Political Science require prior departmental approval; BA students generally cannot take Master''s courses. Cross-registration at HU Berlin, TU Berlin, and University of Potsdam possible with prior lecturer approval."},"credit_system_and_load":{"notes":"Grading scale table detailed on Fact Sheet p.4.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"ECTS (Leistungspunkte/LP); regular full-time workload is 30 ECTS per semester (FU recommends 10-30 ECTS for exchange students; no strict host minimum). Grading scale (except Law): 1.0-1.5 very good, 1.6-2.5 good, 2.6-3.5 satisfactory, 3.5-4.0 sufficient, 5.0 fail."},"cross_references":[],"daily_life_english_friendliness":{"notes":"Not explicitly stated in FU Berlin fact sheets or official fu-berlin.de pages reviewed; left unknown per zero-fabrication rules.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"eligible_auc_schools":{"notes":"Normalized from agreement_scope_raw == ''University-wide'' across merged rows 36-37 (subject exclusions noted in excluded_majors).","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["ALL"]},"eligible_majors":{"notes":"Normalized from agreement_scope_raw == ''University-wide'' across merged rows 36-37 (subject exclusions noted in excluded_majors).","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["ALL"]},"english_course_availability":{"notes":"AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet p.1 states almost all undergraduate subjects are taught in German and English courses outside English/North American Studies are very limited in number (supplemented by Exchange courses and Drive English course snapshots Winter 2024-25 & Summer 2025).","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"limited"},"english_course_list_url":{"notes":"No standalone static live English-only course list URL; use language filter in https://www.fu-berlin.de/vv/en/fb. Past-term Drive snapshots exist in data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/FUB English Courses Winter 2024-25.xlsx & Summer 2025.xlsx.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"english_proficiency_and_rhet1020":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"No general English test certificate stated for most departments; CEFR C1 English level required for courses at the John F. Kennedy Institute for North American Studies."},"est_monthly_living_local":{"notes":"Official FU Berlin Cairo FAQ lists minimum 934 EUR/month (rental fees, groceries, leisure). AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet (#page=2,#page=3) separately cites ERG housing 500-1,200 EUR/month, student health insurance ~150 EUR/month (under age 30), and mandatory semester/social fees ~310 EUR/semester; German federal student visa blocked-account threshold is 992 EUR/month.","source_ref":"https://www.fu-berlin.de/en/sites/cairo/faq/faq-study/living-costs/index.html","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":{"currency":"EUR","max":934,"min":934}},"excel_rows":[36,37],"exchange_page_url":{"notes":"Embedded official incoming Direct Exchange URL in AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet p.1 and verified via fu-berlin.de search.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"https://www.fu-berlin.de/en/studium/international/studium_fu/auslandssemester/direktaustausch_in/index.html"},"excluded_majors":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["Human Medicine","Veterinary Medicine","Fee-based continuing education master''s programs"]},"ext":{},"fact_sheet_status":{"drive_links":["https://drive.google.com/open?id=1wuN41flUPswGwd4J60yc2WHJ_zYAUkTR","https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1s1UPTvrn81gxWfUkqtkfM2cVZ05dJqUB"],"extracted_files":["data/raw/extracted/FUBerlin/2024-2025/Courses/FUB English Courses Summer 2024.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/FUBerlin/2024-2025/Courses/FUB English Courses Winter 2023-24.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/FUBerlin/2024-2025/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2025-2026.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/FUBerlin/26-27/FUB English Courses Summer 2025.xlsx.txt","data/raw/extracted/FUBerlin/26-27/FUB English Courses Winter 2024-25.xlsx.txt","data/raw/extracted/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/FUBerlin/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2022-2023.pdf.txt"],"local_files":["data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/2024-2025/Courses/FUB English Courses Summer 2024.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/2024-2025/Courses/FUB English Courses Winter 2023-24.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/2024-2025/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2025-2026.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/FUB English Courses Summer 2025.xlsx","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/FUB English Courses Winter 2024-25.xlsx","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2022-2023.pdf"],"match_status":"matched","notes":"Col H link (1wuN41flUPswGwd4J60yc2WHJ_zYAUkTR) unreachable (error_html_response: Drive returned HTML page instead of document payload) | Resolved via matching public folder inside Drive master folder"},"fall_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Winter Term 2026/2027: Semester Oct 1, 2026 – Mar 31, 2027; Orientation first week of October; Lecture period Oct 12, 2026 – Feb 19, 2027; Exams typically during last two weeks of lecture period (varies by department)."},"final_semester_allowed":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_grants_or_stipends":{"notes":"PROMOS/DAAD links found via web search apply to outgoing FU Berlin students; no incoming host stipend confirmed for AUC Direct Exchange.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_language_requirement":{"notes":"Optional pre-semester and free in-semester German course details on Fact Sheet p.2.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Exempt from DSH/TestDaF exam and no certificate required (home university verifies); expected German CEFR B2 for Humanities & Social Sciences and B1 for Natural Sciences. Optional pre-semester 6-week intensive German course (~900 EUR, all levels incl. beginners) and free in-semester German courses (placement test required)."},"housing_availability":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"assisted"},"housing_notes":{"notes":"ERG Accommodation Service options, ~500-1,200 EUR/month range, and June 10 / Dec 10 registration deadlines from AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet #page=3; ''no on-campus accommodation available'' corroborated in data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/2024-2025/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2025-2026.pdf#page=3.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"No on-campus accommodation available (per AY 2025-2026 Fact Sheet #page=3). Students may arrange private housing (e.g., WG shared flats) or apply via FU Berlin''s ERG Accommodation Service (dorms, shared apartments, furnished single apartments; ~500-1,200 EUR/month). First-come, first-served; mandatory online registration deadlines June 10 (Winter term) and December 10 (Summer term)."},"instruction_languages":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["German","English"]},"international_support_services":{"notes":"Distributed Campus, Pass Service, German language courses, and Exchange courses detailed across Fact Sheet p.1-p.3.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Mandatory orientation program (5-10 days before lectures: course selection, FU-Net/campus tours), Distributed Campus onboarding portal, Pass Service (arrival residence permit assistance), pre-semester and free in-semester German language courses via ZE Sprachenzentrum, plus dedicated Exchange courses in German culture/history/society."},"living_cost_usd_est":{"notes":"Converted from FU Berlin official minimum monthly estimate of 934 EUR over 5 months: 934 EUR * 5 * FX rate 1.1052 USD/EUR = 5,161.28 USD. FX rate 1 EUR = 1.1052 USD from ECB Euro reference exchange rates for 2026-11-13 (latest prior to 2026-11-15), retrieved 2026-11-15 at https://www.ecb.europa.eu/stats/policy_and_exchange_rates/euro_reference_exchange_rates/html/index.en.html.","source_ref":"https://www.fu-berlin.de/en/sites/cairo/faq/faq-study/living-costs/index.html","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":5161.28},"mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Exempt from university tuition; mandatory semester ticket and social fees ~310 EUR/semester (paid prior to arrival). Mandatory comprehensive German health insurance required for enrollment and residence permit (~150 EUR/month for students under age 30 via German public student insurance; external waivers rarely accepted unless EHIC/GHIC or unlimited coverage)."},"min_gpa_host":{"notes":"AY 2026-2027 incoming Direct Exchange fact sheet specifies no numeric minimum GPA (2.5 GPA in FU web search results refers to FU outgoing students, not incoming exchange).","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"min_standing_note":{"notes":"Application eligibility also summarized on Fact Sheet p.1.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Must be nominated by home university; in general BA students cannot enroll in Master''s programs or individual Master''s-level courses (case-by-case departmental exceptions possible); visiting PhD enrollment possible with prerequisites."},"nomination_deadlines":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Winter term: Nomination & student application deadline April 30; Summer term: Nomination & student application deadline October 30."},"official_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Freie Universität Berlin"},"official_website_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"https://www.fu-berlin.de/en/"},"region":{"notes":"From normalized manifest country/region mapping","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:36,37","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Europe"},"required_application_docs":{"notes":"Nomination and online MoveON application checklist also referenced on Fact Sheet p.1.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["Official home university nomination (email or letter)","Online MoveON application form","Passport photocopy (photo page)","University transcript of records (German or English)","Copies of completed B.A./M.A./other degrees (if available)","Proof of comprehensive German/valid health insurance & semester fee payment (for enrollment)"]},"schema_version":"1.0.0","seat_quota":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"shard":2,"short_name":{"notes":"Official abbreviation used in AY 2026/2027 Fact Sheet header/footer and fu-berlin.de.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"FU Berlin"},"slug":"freie-universitat-berlin","spring_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Summer Term 2027: Semester Apr 1, 2027 – Sep 30, 2027; Orientation first week of April; Lecture period Apr 12, 2027 – Jul 23, 2027; Exams typically during last two weeks of lecture period (varies by department)."},"state_or_province":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"tuition_model":{"notes":"Fact Sheet p.2 states exchange students are exempt from university tuition fees, though mandatory semester ticket and social fees still apply.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"auc_exchange_waiver"},"visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof":{"notes":"Pre-arrival entry visa requirement & >=8 weeks visa processing from AY 2026-2027 Fact Sheet #page=2; Berlin residence permit 8-14 week timeline from https://www.fu-berlin.de/en/studium/international/studium_fu/einreise_aufenthalt/aufenthaltserlaubnis/index.html; blocked account 992 EUR/mo (11,904 EUR/yr) from https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/sperrkonto/388600; FU >=934 EUR/mo baseline from https://www.fu-berlin.de/en/sites/cairo/faq/faq-study/living-costs/index.html.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/FUBerlin/26-27/Fact Sheet Direct Exchange Program FU Berlin academic year 2026-2027.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":"Non-EU/EEA/non-exempt nationals (incl. Egypt) must obtain a German student visa prior to arrival (processing takes at least 8 weeks, up to several months, per Fact Sheet #page=2). After arrival, non-EU students apply for a Berlin residence permit (Aufenthaltserlaubnis) via LEA/FU Pass-Service (typically 8 to 14 weeks processing). Financial proof (e.g., blocked account / Sperrkonto) required per German Federal Foreign Office standard (992 EUR/month / 11,904 EUR/year; FU Berlin general FAQ lists >=934 EUR/month)."}}');
