 test required for partner universities'' exchange students. No RHET 1020 waiver stated.', NULL, '["Fall","Spring","Summer"]', 'AY 2025-2026: Term incl. exams Aug 25 – Dec 21, 2025 (arrival preferred Aug 19; mandatory orientation Aug 21–22).', 'AY 2025-2026: Term incl. exams Jan 7 – May 31, 2026 (arrival Jan 2; orientation Jan 5–6).', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'EUR', 900.0, 1850.0, 7598.25, 'partial', 'OFII fiscal stamp €50; accommodation insurance €59/yr + civil liability insurance; ALL card €11 (Lille). Non-EU students register for free French Social Security (Ameli) and must provide a pre-arrival doctor medical attestation with vaccination record.', 'assisted', 'Estimated rent: Lille €450–€800/month (avg €600); Paris €600–€1,200/month (avg €850). CAF housing subsidy may apply after arrival.', 'French CAF housing subsidy (€30–€250/month possible for stays >=90 days with valid residence title and French bank account; 2+ months processing).', NULL, 'VLS-TS long-stay student visa required for >90 days (Schengen if <90 days), Campus France procedure where applicable, plus €50 OFII validation stamp post-arrival.', 'http://www.ieseg.fr/en/', 'https://www.ieseg.fr/en/international/study-at-ieseg-in-exchange/', 'https://www.ieseg.fr/en/international/study-at-ieseg-in-exchange/course-list/', 'https://www.ieseg.fr/en/international/study-at-ieseg-in-exchange/course-list/', 'ECTS; regular load 30 ECTS (8–12 courses), minimum 20 ECTS; French 0–20 grading scale (10/20 pass); no retake exams for exchange students.', 'Exchange restricted to Grande Ecole Program only. Bachelor students take Semester 6 (4th-year BA students may choose BA or Master); Master students take Master courses; no course changes after Learning Agreement signed.', '["Online application (https://candidate.ieseg.fr/)","ID photo","Official university transcripts","Passport or EU ID card copy","CV / resume","Learning Agreement (submitted after course selection)"]', NULL, NULL, 'multi_campus', NULL, 'Man