undergraduate students and 3.0/4.0 for graduate students (individual departments may enforce higher thresholds); in-person course enrollment at the Kent Campus required.', 'University-wide', '["ALL"]', '["ALL"]', NULL, 2.0, '["English"]', 'full', 'Undergraduate baseline: TOEFL iBT 71, IELTS Academic 6.0, Duolingo 100, or PTE Academic 48. Graduate baseline: TOEFL iBT 71 / IELTS 6.0 (specific programs may require higher). RHET 1020 waiver not stated.', 'English proficiency required (see english_proficiency_and_rhet1020).', '["Fall","Spring"]', '2026-08-24 to 2026-12-20 (classes Aug 24–Dec 13; final exams Dec 14–20, 2026)', '2027-01-19 to 2027-05-09 (classes Jan 19–May 9, 2027 including finals)', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'USD', 1830, 1830, 9147.5, 'partial', 'KSU Student Health Insurance Plan (UHCSR SHIP) is mandatory for all international exchange students and cannot be waived. Mandatory fees: $20/sem international activity fee, $100 first-semester orientation fee, plus UG fees ($15/sem arts, $93.84/sem career services, $90/sem student health); $10/transcript fee.', 'assisted', '2026-2027 double residence hall rate approx. $4,335/semester (https://www.kent.edu/housing/room-rates); recommended Blue Meal Plan $5,690/year (~$2,845/sem per https://www.kent.edu/dining/meal-plans); seasonal break housing $35/night (`KSU Fact Sheet 2026-2027.pdf#page=3`).', NULL, NULL, 'J-1 Exchange Visitor visa (Form DS-2019) required for non-US students; 2026-2027 proof of financial support for exchange students is $9,147.50 USD (1 semester) or $18,295 USD (2 semesters).', 'https://www.kent.edu/', 'https://www.kent.edu/globaleducation', 'https://catalog.kent.edu/coursesaz/', NULL, 'US credit hours: UG 12–18 credits/semester; GR 8–18 credits/semester. Excess credits beyond 18 incur standard per-credit tuition charges.', 'Students must enroll in in-person courses at the Kent Campus; some programs and courses are not available to international exchange students or at the Kent Campus.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Office of Global Education orientation, J-1 visa support, housing/dining coordination, and DeWeese Health Center.', 'Fall Semester or Academic Year: nomination March 1, application April 1. Spring Semester: nomination October 1, application October 15 (KSU Florence deadlines earlier: Sep 15 / Oct 1).', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:57","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"University-wide"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:57","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:57","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG","GR"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"Fall/Spring","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:57","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Fall","Spring"]},"campus_type":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:57","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Kent"},"city_tier":{"notes":"Flagship Kent Campus sits in Kent, Ohio (~28,000 residents per kent.edu); left unknown rather than assuming city_tier label.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"country":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:57","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"United States"},"course_catalog_url":{"no