st submit IELTS Academic 6.5 (no band <6.0), TOEFL iBT/Home Edition 88 (min 20 in Writing, Speaking, Reading, and Listening; code 0949), Duolingo 120, CAEL 70, PTE 60, or Cambridge 175 (Smith #page=2 also lists TOEFL PBT 580). Exempt with IB diploma (excl. SL English B alone) or >=3 years residency in an English-primary country or full-time study in an English-medium institution. RHET 1020 waiver not stated.', 'English proficiency required unless exempt via 3+ years English-medium instruction.', '["Fall","Spring"]', '2026-09-08 to 2026-12-23 (Mandatory orientation Sep 4; classes Sep 8–Dec 8; exams Dec 10–23, 2026)', '2027-01-15 to 2027-04-23 (Winter term: classes Jan 15–Apr 5; exams Apr 9–23, 2027; orientation Jan 2027)', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'CAD', 1560, 2250, 6680.4, 'partial', 'Mandatory automatic enrollment in University Health Insurance Plan (UHIP) for international/exchange students (~CAD $264/1 term or CAD $528/2 terms per 2026-27 factsheets; transcripts held if UHIP balance owed). Student card includes Kingston Transit.', 'off_campus_only', 'Off-campus rentals only (est. CAD $720–$1,380/month incl. utilities); supported by Queen''s Off-Campus Living Advisor (OCLA) and Queen''s University International Centre (QUIC).', NULL, NULL, 'Single-semester exchange (<6 months) can enter as a visitor (TRV or eTA, no Canadian Study Permit required); stays of 6 months or more (full-year) require a Canadian Study Permit.', 'https://www.queensu.ca/', 'https://www.queensu.ca/international/incoming-exchange/costs', NULL, NULL, 'Queen''s credit units (3.0 units = 1 one-term course; 6.0 units = full-year course). Standard full-time load: 12.0–15.0 units (4–5 courses) per semester; 4.3 GPA grading scale.', 'Arts & Science excludes History (300-level+) and Political Studies (300-level+) and limits high-demand subjects (e.g., Economics, Psychology, Sociology).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'International Programs Office (IPO), Queen''s University International Centre (QUIC), Off-Campus Living Advisor (OCLA), Orientation, and free transcript dispatch (if account clear).', 'Fall / Full Year: nomination April 1, application April 30. Winter: early nomination April 1 / final nomination September 1, final application September 30 (fixed annual dates).', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:90","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"BUS, Law, arts&science"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:90","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:90","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"AUC Spring corresponds to Queen''s Winter term (January–April).","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:90","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Fall","Spring"]},"campus_type":{"notes":"Arts & Science Fact Sheet describes a campus-based university ~10-minute walk from downtown Kingston; left unknown rather than assuming urban vs suburban.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:90","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Kingston"},"city_tier":{"notes":"Smith Commerce 2026-27 Fact Sheet describes Kingston as a \"small size city\"; left unknown rather than guessing college_town vs mid_size_city.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"country":{"notes"