us Opening Session, Welcome Week & Mentoring Academy, ESN Bragança buddy/housing support, and intensive/semester Portuguese language course (3 ECTS)."},"living_cost_usd_est":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/The Polytechnic Institute of Braganca/The Polytechnic Institute of Braganca.docx","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Mandatory student accident/health insurance required upon registration (no tuition fee for mobility students)."},"min_gpa_host":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"min_standing_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"nomination_deadlines":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/The Polytechnic Institute of Braganca/The Polytechnic Institute of Braganca.docx","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":"2020-2021 Fact Sheet application windows: Autumn Mar 1-Jul 1; Spring Sep 1-Dec 1 (nominations prior by home IRO)."},"official_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:115","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"The Polytechnic Institute of Braganca"},"official_website_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:115","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"http://portal3.ipb.pt/index.php/en/ipben/home"},"region":{"notes":"From normalized manifest country/region mapping","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:115","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Europe"},"required_application_docs":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"schema_version":"1.0.0","seat_quota":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"shard":7,"short_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://ipb.pt","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"IPB"},"slug":"the-polytechnic-institute-of-braganca","spring_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://portal3.ipb.pt/index.php/en/study/students/academic-services/academic-calendar","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":"2nd Semester (Spring): Runs mid-February through June/July (~19 weeks)."},"state_or_province":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"tuition_model":{"notes":"2020-2021 fact sheet states no tuition fee for mobility students.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/The Polytechnic Institute of Braganca/The Polytechnic Institute of Braganca.docx","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"auc_exchange_waiver"},"visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://ipb.pt","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":"Non-EU/EEA students must obtain a Portuguese Study Visa from the Portuguese Embassy/Consulate before arrival using IPB''s acceptance letter, proof of financial means, valid health insurance, and accommodation details. Lead time not specified."}}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO universities (slug, excel_rows_json, shard, fact_sheet_match_status, fact_sheet_files_json, cross_references_json, official_name, short_name, country, state_or_province, city, region, agreement_status, agreement_student_levels_json, min_standing_note, agreement_scope_raw, eligible_auc_schools_json, eligible_majors_json, excluded_majors_json, min_gpa_host, instruction_languages_json, english_course_availability, english_proficiency_and_rhet1020, host_language_requirement, available_terms_json, fall_term_dates, spring_term_dates, final_semester_allowed, seat_quota, tuition_model, est_monthly_living_currency, est_monthly_living_min, est_monthly_living_max, living_cost_usd_est, living_cost_usd_est_status, mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance, housing_availability, housing_notes, host_grants_or_stipends, citizenship_restrictions, visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof, official_website_url, exchange_page_url, course_catalog_url, english_course_list_url, credit_system_and_load, course_restrictions_note, required_application_docs_json, academic_style, city_tier, campus_type, daily_life_english_friendliness, international_support_services, nomination_deadlines, ext_json, metadata_json) VALUES ('the-university-of-akron', '[116]', 8, 'matched', '["data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.docx","data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf"]', '[]', 'The University of Akron', NULL, 'United States', 'Ohio', 'Akron', 'North America', 'active', '["UG"]', 'Good academic standing with minimum 2.5/4.0 GPA and at least 2 semesters of full-time university study completed prior to enrollment.', 'University-wide', '["ALL"]', '["ALL"]', NULL, 2.5, '["English"]', 'full', 'Undergraduate minimum: TOEFL iBT 71 or IELTS Academic 6.0 (see Proof of English Proficiency at https://uakron.edu/international/apply/). RHET 1020 waiver not stated.', 'English proficiency required (TOEFL iBT 71 or IELTS 6.0).', '["Fall","Spring"]', '2026-08-24 to 2026-12-13 (classes begin Aug 24; final exams Dec 7–13, 2026)', '2027-01-11 to 2027-05-09 (classes begin Jan 11; Spring recess Mar 22–28; final exams May 3–9, 2027)', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'USD', 1588, 1588, 7938.0, 'partial', 'Mandatory international student health insurance (LewerMark, ~$1,328/year per health-insurance.dot unless waived; Spring 2022 factsheet listed $736/sem); SEVIS fee ($220) and J-1 visa fee ($160). No UA application fee.', 'guaranteed', 'On-campus residence hall and meal plan mandatory for exchange students (no exceptions on Spring 2022 factsheet); recent room & board ~$13,317–$13,396/academic year (`tuition-scholarships.dot` & `cost-of-attendance.dot`).', NULL, NULL, 'J-1 Exchange Visitor visa (Form DS-2019) required; financial documents required after acceptance ($220 SEVIS + $160 J-1 visa fees).', 'https://www.uakron.edu/', 'https://www.uakron.edu/international/', 'https://bulletin.uakron.edu/undergraduate/courses-instruction/', NULL, 'US credit hours: 12 to 18 undergraduate credits per semester covered under exchange tuition waiver.', 'Not all catalog courses run every semester; courses with prerequisites require proof of equivalent prior coursework or departmental advisor permission.', '["UA online application (select UA Application, not Common App; placeholder SSN 999-99-9999)","Official transcript emailed directly from home school official to intlrecruit@uakron.edu","Proof of English language proficiency","Passport biographical page (submitted with coordinator nomination)","Financial documentation for DS-2019 (after acceptance)"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'International Center advising, UANet ID onboarding, orientation, and pre-arrival planning (https://www.uakron.edu/international/plan/).', 'Fall / Academic Year application: May 1. Spring nomination: October 15; Spring application: November 1 (consecutive Fall+Spring AY only; no summer exchange).', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"University-wide"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"Fall/Spring","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Fall","Spring"]},"campus_type":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Akron"},"city_tier":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"country":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"United States"},"course_catalog_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"https://bulletin.uakron.edu/undergraduate/courses-instruction/"},"course_restrictions_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Not all catalog courses run every semester; courses with prerequisites require proof of equivalent prior coursework or departmental advisor permission."},"credit_system_and_load":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"US credit hours: 12 to 18 undergraduate credits per semester covered under exchange tuition waiver."},"cross_references":[],"daily_life_english_friendliness":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"eligible_auc_schools":{"notes":"Excel agreement_scope_raw is ''University-wide''.","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["ALL"]},"eligible_majors":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["ALL"]},"english_course_availability":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://uakron.edu/international/apply/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"full"},"english_course_list_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"english_proficiency_and_rhet1020":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://uakron.edu/international/apply/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Undergraduate minimum: TOEFL iBT 71 or IELTS Academic 6.0 (see Proof of English Proficiency at https://uakron.edu/international/apply/). RHET 1020 waiver not stated."},"est_monthly_living_local":{"notes":"Derived as $7,938 / 5 months = $1,587.60/mo (rounded to $1,588) from half of UA international I-20 living estimate ($13,317 room & board + $2,559 books/personal = $15,876/yr, excluding $1,328 insurance). Spring 2022 factsheet (#page=3) listed $5,610/sem room & board + $500/sem books.","source_ref":"https://www.uakron.edu/international/future-students/tuition-scholarships.dot","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":{"currency":"USD","max":1588,"min":1588}},"excel_rows":[116],"exchange_page_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://www.uakron.edu/international/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"https://www.uakron.edu/international/"},"excluded_majors":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"ext":{},"fact_sheet_status":{"drive_links":["https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1VYRymN3qrBbb2CO3Tz1xpoorOg7WDUuf"],"extracted_files":["data/raw/extracted/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.docx.txt","data/raw/extracted/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf.txt"],"local_files":["data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.docx","data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf"],"match_status":"matched","notes":"Excel Col H blank, but matching public folder found in Drive master folder"},"fall_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://www.uakron.edu/calendar/academic-calendar","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"2026-08-24 to 2026-12-13 (classes begin Aug 24; final exams Dec 7–13, 2026)"},"final_semester_allowed":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_grants_or_stipends":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_language_requirement":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://uakron.edu/international/apply/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"English proficiency required (TOEFL iBT 71 or IELTS 6.0)."},"housing_availability":{"notes":"Spring 2022 Fact Sheet mandates: ''Must agree to live on campus and purchase a campus meal plan. UA does not offer exceptions to this requirement for exchange students.''","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":"guaranteed"},"housing_notes":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://www.uakron.edu/finaid/cost-of-attendance.dot","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":"On-campus residence hall and meal plan mandatory for exchange students (no exceptions on Spring 2022 factsheet); recent room & board ~$13,317–$13,396/academic year (`tuition-scholarships.dot` & `cost-of-attendance.dot`)."},"instruction_languages":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://uakron.edu/international/apply/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":["English"]},"international_support_services":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"International Center advising, UANet ID onboarding, orientation, and pre-arrival planning (https://www.uakron.edu/international/plan/)."},"living_cost_usd_est":{"notes":"1-semester USD estimate derived as half of annual international student Room & Board ($13,317) + Books & Personal Expenses ($2,559) = $7,938.00 USD (excluding health insurance ~$1,328/yr; already in USD, recorded 2026-11-15).","source_ref":"https://www.uakron.edu/international/future-students/tuition-scholarships.dot","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":7938.0},"mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance":{"notes":"SEVIS/J-1 and zero application fee also confirmed in Spring 2022 Fact Sheet #page=2–3.","source_ref":"https://www.uakron.edu/international/current-students/health-insurance.dot","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Mandatory international student health insurance (LewerMark, ~$1,328/year per health-insurance.dot unless waived; Spring 2022 factsheet listed $736/sem); SEVIS fee ($220) and J-1 visa fee ($160). No UA application fee."},"min_gpa_host":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":2.5},"min_standing_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Good academic standing with minimum 2.5/4.0 GPA and at least 2 semesters of full-time university study completed prior to enrollment."},"nomination_deadlines":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Fall / Academic Year application: May 1. Spring nomination: October 15; Spring application: November 1 (consecutive Fall+Spring AY only; no summer exchange)."},"official_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"The University of Akron"},"official_website_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"https://www.uakron.edu/"},"region":{"notes":"From normalized manifest country/region mapping","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"North America"},"required_application_docs":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["UA online application (select UA Application, not Common App; placeholder SSN 999-99-9999)","Official transcript emailed directly from home school official to intlrecruit@uakron.edu","Proof of English language proficiency","Passport biographical page (submitted with coordinator nomination)","Financial documentation for DS-2019 (after acceptance)"]},"schema_version":"1.0.0","seat_quota":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"shard":8,"short_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"slug":"the-university-of-akron","spring_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://www.uakron.edu/calendar/academic-calendar","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"2027-01-11 to 2027-05-09 (classes begin Jan 11; Spring recess Mar 22–28; final exams May 3–9, 2027)"},"state_or_province":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:116","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Ohio"},"tuition_model":{"notes":"Tuition and fees are waived for incoming exchange students (12 to 18 undergraduate credits).","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"auc_exchange_waiver"},"visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof":{"notes":"Fees noted on #page=3; pre-arrival guidance at https://www.uakron.edu/international/plan/.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/University of Akron/UoAkron Exchange Partner Fact Spring 2022.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"J-1 Exchange Visitor visa (Form DS-2019) required; financial documents required after acceptance ($220 SEVIS + $160 J-1 visa fees)."}}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO universities (slug, excel_rows_json, shard, fact_sheet_match_status, fact_sheet_files_json, cross_references_json, official_name, short_name, country, state_or_province, city, region, agreement_status, agreement_student_levels_json, min_standing_note, agreement_scope_raw, eligible_auc_schools_json, eligible_majors_json, excluded_majors_json, min_gpa_host, instruction_languages_json, english_course_availability, english_proficiency_and_rhet1020, host_language_requirement, available_terms_json, fall_term_dates, spring_term_dates, final_semester_allowed, seat_quota, tuition_model, est_monthly_living_currency, est_monthly_living_min, est_monthly_living_max, living_cost_usd_est, living_cost_usd_est_status, mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance, housing_availability, housing_notes, host_grants_or_stipends, citizenship_restrictions, visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof, official_website_url, exchange_page_url, course_catalog_url, english_course_list_url, credit_system_and_load, course_restrictions_note, required_application_docs_json, academic_style, city_tier, campus_type, daily_life_english_friendliness, international_support_services, nomination_deadlines, ext_json, metadata_json) VALUES ('the-university-of-kansas', '[117]', 1, 'matched', '["data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/2026 Undergraduate Exchange Application instructions.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2025.pdf"]', '[]', 'The University of Kansas', 'KU', 'United States', 'Kansas', 'Lawrence', 'North America', 'active', '["UG","GR"]', 'Incoming exchange students must be officially nominated by their home university and remain in good academic standing as non-degree seeking study abroad students.', 'University-wide', '["ALL"]', '["ALL"]', '["Athletic Training","Law","Medicine","Pharmacy"]', NULL, '["English"]', 'full', 'TOEFL and IELTS scores are NOT required to apply for exchange at KU; however, all non-native English speakers must take the Applied English Center (AEC) English Proficiency Exam (online pre-arrival or at orientation) unless waived by TOEFL iBT >=79 (no subscore <18 UG / <23/section Grad) or IELTS >=6.5 (no subscore <6.0). Note ''Assessment of Functional Level of English'' J-1 form does NOT waive the AEC exam. RHET 1020 exemption not mentioned.', NULL, '["Fall","Spring"]', 'Fall 2026: Orientation Arrival Date 10 Aug 2026; Classes begin 24 Aug 2026; Labor Day 7 Sep; Fall Break 17–20 Oct; Thanksgiving Break 25–29 Nov; Final Exams end 18 Dec 2026 (https://registrar.ku.edu/calendar).', 'Spring 2027: Orientation Arrival Date 11 Jan 2027; MLK Day 18 Jan; Classes begin 19 Jan 2027; Spring Break 15–21 Mar 2027; Final Exams end 13 May 2027 (https://registrar.ku.edu/calendar).', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'USD', 2047, 2047, 10235.56, 'partial', 'Students pay mandatory UnitedHealthcare health insurance (~USD 1,180/semester unless waived via https://iss.ku.edu/waivers by 1st day of class), Orientation Fee (USD 290), ISS Check-In Fee (USD 40), and KUID card (USD 21) — billed after arrival/enrollment.', 'assisted', 'Exchange students arrange their own housing once admitted with KUID (https://housing.ku.edu; early move-in ~$40/night). On-campus options: apartments (Jayhawker Towers, Stouffer, McCarthy — open over breaks, optional dining) or Residence Halls (GSP, Corbin, Ellsworth, Hashinger open to all levels; mandatory dining plan at https://union.ku.edu/dining-plans; closed Winter Break unless extra fee paid). Fall-only students can opt out of Spring from AY contracts free of charge. Off-campus adjacent alternative: Naismith Hall (https://www.naismithhall.com/).', NULL, NULL, 'J-1 Exchange Visitor (student) DS-2019 required; must arrive no later than DS-2019 Start Date (= Orientation Arrival Date). Proof of financial support must cover the ENTIRE J-1 duration using bank statements/letters <6 months old or sponsorship letters (+ signed Affidavit of Financial Support if not student''s own funds) per https://iss.ku.edu/proof-finances and Fact Sheet #page=2,4.', 'https://www.ku.edu/', 'https://studyabroad.ku.edu/exchangestudents', 'https://classes.ku.edu', NULL, 'US semester credit hours. Exchange students must enroll full-time within exact caps: Undergraduates 12–15 credits/semester (typically 4–5 classes); Graduates 9 credits/semester (up to 12 max). Exceeding 15 UG / 12 Grad credits triggers direct tuition/fee charges; max 1 online course/semester.', 'Enrollment blocked until AEC English test/waiver, ''You at KU'' orientation registration, and health check-in appointment are completed. Must select Lawrence campus courses only (KU Med/Edwards/Regents prohibited), avoid Athletic Training/Law/Medicine/Pharmacy, and submit >=2 alternate courses. Independent Study/research credit typically unavailable; portfolios/auditions may apply for Architecture/Design/Art/Music.', '["Online ''KU Non-Degree Study Abroad'' application via https://world.ku.edu/apply (enter exchange fee waiver code 42626669ku)","Official current university transcript + list of courses in progress","Copy of passport","Evidence of financial support","Assessment of Functional Level of English form (for J-1 DS-2019)","English test score report (optional, for AEC exam waiver)","Portfolio or audition (Architecture, Design, Visual Art, or Music only)"]', 'Comprehensive US AAU research university (~30,000 students, ~200 majors) on 950-acre Mount Oread campus in Lawrence, KS; classes may combine large lectures with LAB/DIS sections; AEC coursework offered if English placement requires.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Mandatory ''You at KU'' orientation via ISS (https://iss.ku.edu/newly-admitted-students) including immigration check-in, shuttled shopping excursions, and social activities (#page=4); Applied English Center (https://studyabroad.ku.edu/applied-english-center); Campus Fee covers recreation/fitness center, campus bus, library, health center, >500 student groups (#page=1,5).', 'Fall / Full Academic Year: Nomination 1 March (at least 2 weeks pre-app) / Application 15 March; Spring: Nomination 1 October / Application 15 October.', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":"950-acre Mount Oread campus figure confirmed on ku.edu.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Comprehensive US AAU research university (~30,000 students, ~200 majors) on 950-acre Mount Oread campus in Lawrence, KS; classes may combine large lectures with LAB/DIS sections; AEC coursework offered if English placement requires."},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"University-wide"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG","GR"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"Fall/Spring","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Fall","Spring"]},"campus_type":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Lawrence"},"city_tier":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"country":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"United States"},"course_catalog_url":{"notes":"Academics overview: https://www.ku.edu/academics/","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"https://classes.ku.edu"},"course_restrictions_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Enrollment blocked until AEC English test/waiver, ''You at KU'' orientation registration, and health check-in appointment are completed. Must select Lawrence campus courses only (KU Med/Edwards/Regents prohibited), avoid Athletic Training/Law/Medicine/Pharmacy, and submit >=2 alternate courses. Independent Study/research credit typically unavailable; portfolios/auditions may apply for Architecture/Design/Art/Music."},"credit_system_and_load":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"US semester credit hours. Exchange students must enroll full-time within exact caps: Undergraduates 12–15 credits/semester (typically 4–5 classes); Graduates 9 credits/semester (up to 12 max). Exceeding 15 UG / 12 Grad credits triggers direct tuition/fee charges; max 1 online course/semester."},"cross_references":[],"daily_life_english_friendliness":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"eligible_auc_schools":{"notes":"University-wide Excel agreement; AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=3 excludes Athletic Training, Law, Medicine, and Pharmacy, and restricts courses to Lawrence campus only.","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"partial","value":["ALL"]},"eligible_majors":{"notes":"Nearly 200 fields of study (Architecture/Design/Planning, Arts, Business, Engineering, Journalism & Mass Comm, Liberal Arts & Sciences, Music, Applied English Center per #page=1), excluding restricted health/law fields.","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"partial","value":["ALL"]},"english_course_availability":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"full"},"english_course_list_url":{"notes":"All KU regular coursework at classes.ku.edu is in English.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"english_proficiency_and_rhet1020":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"TOEFL and IELTS scores are NOT required to apply for exchange at KU; however, all non-native English speakers must take the Applied English Center (AEC) English Proficiency Exam (online pre-arrival or at orientation) unless waived by TOEFL iBT >=79 (no subscore <18 UG / <23/section Grad) or IELTS >=6.5 (no subscore <6.0). Note ''Assessment of Functional Level of English'' J-1 form does NOT waive the AEC exam. RHET 1020 exemption not mentioned."},"est_monthly_living_local":{"notes":"Derived from KU International Admissions annual international undergraduate living expenses budget USD 18,424/yr (housing, food, personal items, books, mandatory health insurance) divided over 9 academic months = USD 2,047.11/month.","source_ref":"https://world.ku.edu/costs","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":{"currency":"USD","max":2047,"min":2047}},"excel_rows":[117],"exchange_page_url":{"notes":"Also verified via search_web.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=5","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"https://studyabroad.ku.edu/exchangestudents"},"excluded_majors":{"notes":"AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=3 also states exchange students may only take courses at the Lawrence campus (excluding KU Med, Edwards, and Regents campuses) and Independent Study/research credit is typically unavailable.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["Athletic Training","Law","Medicine","Pharmacy"]},"ext":{},"fact_sheet_status":{"drive_links":["https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1E0mfllVPRBHJNPK5EDpGLJ6EREqKbhBf"],"extracted_files":["data/raw/extracted/Kansas University/2026 Undergraduate Exchange Application instructions.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf.txt","data/raw/extracted/Kansas University/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2025.pdf.txt"],"local_files":["data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/2026 Undergraduate Exchange Application instructions.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2025.pdf"],"match_status":"matched","notes":null},"fall_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Fall 2026: Orientation Arrival Date 10 Aug 2026; Classes begin 24 Aug 2026; Labor Day 7 Sep; Fall Break 17–20 Oct; Thanksgiving Break 25–29 Nov; Final Exams end 18 Dec 2026 (https://registrar.ku.edu/calendar)."},"final_semester_allowed":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_grants_or_stipends":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"host_language_requirement":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"housing_availability":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"assisted"},"housing_notes":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Exchange students arrange their own housing once admitted with KUID (https://housing.ku.edu; early move-in ~$40/night). On-campus options: apartments (Jayhawker Towers, Stouffer, McCarthy — open over breaks, optional dining) or Residence Halls (GSP, Corbin, Ellsworth, Hashinger open to all levels; mandatory dining plan at https://union.ku.edu/dining-plans; closed Winter Break unless extra fee paid). Fall-only students can opt out of Spring from AY contracts free of charge. Off-campus adjacent alternative: Naismith Hall (https://www.naismithhall.com/)."},"instruction_languages":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["English"]},"international_support_services":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Mandatory ''You at KU'' orientation via ISS (https://iss.ku.edu/newly-admitted-students) including immigration check-in, shuttled shopping excursions, and social activities (#page=4); Applied English Center (https://studyabroad.ku.edu/applied-english-center); Campus Fee covers recreation/fitness center, campus bus, library, health center, >500 student groups (#page=1,5)."},"living_cost_usd_est":{"notes":"5-month USD estimate derived from KU International Admissions annual living expenses budget USD 18,424/yr (USD 2,047.11/mo over 9 months x 5 = USD 10,235.56; 1-semester half share = USD 9,212), verified 2026-11-15 (USD local currency; no FX conversion).","source_ref":"https://world.ku.edu/costs","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":10235.56},"mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=5","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Students pay mandatory UnitedHealthcare health insurance (~USD 1,180/semester unless waived via https://iss.ku.edu/waivers by 1st day of class), Orientation Fee (USD 290), ISS Check-In Fee (USD 40), and KUID card (USD 21) — billed after arrival/enrollment."},"min_gpa_host":{"notes":"No minimum incoming exchange GPA stated in AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet (the 2.5 GPA on #page=2 applies solely to an English-proficiency test waiver for students who graduated from an English-language high school; 2.5 on KU Study Abroad pages applies to outgoing KU students).","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"min_standing_note":{"notes":"Official partner nomination rule also on AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=2.","source_ref":"https://studyabroad.ku.edu/exchangestudents","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"Incoming exchange students must be officially nominated by their home university and remain in good academic standing as non-degree seeking study abroad students."},"nomination_deadlines":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Fall / Full Academic Year: Nomination 1 March (at least 2 weeks pre-app) / Application 15 March; Spring: Nomination 1 October / Application 15 October."},"official_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"The University of Kansas"},"official_website_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"https://www.ku.edu/"},"region":{"notes":"From normalized manifest country/region mapping","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"North America"},"required_application_docs":{"notes":"Fee waiver code 42626669ku and online portal steps confirmed in 2026 UG Application Instructions #page=1-5.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":["Online ''KU Non-Degree Study Abroad'' application via https://world.ku.edu/apply (enter exchange fee waiver code 42626669ku)","Official current university transcript + list of courses in progress","Copy of passport","Evidence of financial support","Assessment of Functional Level of English form (for J-1 DS-2019)","English test score report (optional, for AEC exam waiver)","Portfolio or audition (Architecture, Design, Visual Art, or Music only)"]},"schema_version":"1.0.0","seat_quota":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"shard":1,"short_name":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"KU"},"slug":"the-university-of-kansas","spring_term_dates":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Spring 2027: Orientation Arrival Date 11 Jan 2027; MLK Day 18 Jan; Classes begin 19 Jan 2027; Spring Break 15–21 Mar 2027; Final Exams end 13 May 2027 (https://registrar.ku.edu/calendar)."},"state_or_province":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:117","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Kansas"},"tuition_model":{"notes":"AY 2026-27 Fact Sheet #page=5 confirms Tuition, Course Fees, Technology Fee, International Student Service Fee, Infrastructure Fee, Wellness Fee, and Campus Fee are covered by KU Study Abroad & Global Engagement (exchange application fee also waived via code 42626669ku in 2026 UG Application Instructions #page=1).","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=5","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"auc_exchange_waiver"},"visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof":{"notes":"Also cites #page=2 (financial docs), 2026 UG Application Instructions #page=4 (select J-1 Exchange Visitor), and https://iss.ku.edu/proof-finances.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Kansas University/Fact Sheet 2026-27/KU Exchange Fact Sheet 2026-27.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"J-1 Exchange Visitor (student) DS-2019 required; must arrive no later than DS-2019 Start Date (= Orientation Arrival Date). Proof of financial support must cover the ENTIRE J-1 duration using bank statements/letters <6 months old or sponsorship letters (+ signed Affidavit of Financial Support if not student''s own funds) per https://iss.ku.edu/proof-finances and Fact Sheet #page=2,4."}}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO universities (slug, excel_rows_json, shard, fact_sheet_match_status, fact_sheet_files_json, cross_references_json, official_name, short_name, country, state_or_province, city, region, agreement_status, agreement_student_levels_json, min_standing_note, agreement_scope_raw, eligible_auc_schools_json, eligible_majors_json, excluded_majors_json, min_gpa_host, instruction_languages_json, english_course_availability, english_proficiency_and_rhet1020, host_language_requirement, available_terms_json, fall_term_dates, spring_term_dates, final_semester_allowed, seat_quota, tuition_model, est_monthly_living_currency, est_monthly_living_min, est_monthly_living_max, living_cost_usd_est, living_cost_usd_est_status, mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance, housing_availability, housing_notes, host_grants_or_stipends, citizenship_restrictions, visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof, official_website_url, exchange_page_url, course_catalog_url, english_course_list_url, credit_system_and_load, course_restrictions_note, required_application_docs_json, academic_style, city_tier, campus_type, daily_life_english_friendliness, international_support_services, nomination_deadlines, ext_json, metadata_json) VALUES ('the-university-of-new-mexico', '[118]', 2, 'matched', '["data/raw/factsheets/New Mexico/2021- 2022/University of New Mexico Exchange Flyer.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/TUo New Mexico/Copy of University of New Mexico Information Sheet 2021-2022 (1).pdf","data/raw/factsheets/TUo New Mexico/UNM Information Sheet 2025-2026.pdf"]', '[]', 'The University of New Mexico', 'UNM', 'United States', 'New Mexico', 'Albuquerque', 'North America', 'active', '["UG","GR"]', 'Exchange students exempt from English tests if having >=1 yr full-time study at an English-medium university; UG/GR eligible per agreement.', 'University-wide', '["ALL"]', '["ALL"]', '["School of Medicine","Nursing","Pharmacy"]', 3.0, '["English"]', 'full', 'Exempt if attending a university where English is the medium of instruction for >=1 year full-time (applies to AUC) or qualifying HS diploma <=2 yrs old. Otherwise: UG TOEFL iBT 68 / IELTS 6.0 / PTE 47 / Duolingo 95 / C1-C2 169; GR iBT 79 / IELTS 6.5 / PTE 53 / Duolingo 105 / C1-C2 176; Law School TOEFL iBT 100.', 'English only.', '["Fall","Spring","Summer"]', 'AY 2026-2027 Fall Semester: Classes Aug 17 - Dec 12, 2026 (Fall Break Oct 8-9, 2026); arrive >=1 week prior for orientation (Fact Sheet p.2).', 'AY 2026-2027 Spring Semester: Classes Jan 18 - May 15, 2027 (Spring Break Mar 14-21, 2027); arrive >=1 week prior (Fact Sheet p.2).', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'USD', 1782, 1964, 9365.0, 'partial', 'Per semester: Visa Processing & Admin Fee $275, Mandatory IT Fee $50, Department/Upper-Division Course Fees $25-$400 per class, plus mandatory UNM-negotiated International Student Health Insurance (non-US citizens; emergency coverage only) and US Gov SEVIS fee.', 'assisted', 'On-campus housing and off-campus listings provided on Fact Sheet p.6 (Housing & Food AY 2026-27 estimate $10,648-$12,471 on unm.edu COA).', NULL, 'US citizens cannot purchase UNM International Student Health Insurance (contact exchange@unm.edu).', 'J-1 Visa requires liquid financial proof (<6 months old; no loans/credit cards/investments): $7,500 (1 semester), $15,000 (Academic Year Aug-May), $17,500 (Calendar Year Jan-Dec), or $4,375 (Summer), plus US SEVIS fee.', 'http://www.unm.edu/', 'https://studyabroad.unm.edu/exchange', 'https://registrar.unm.edu/UNM%20Catalog/index.html', NULL, 'US semester credits (3 cr = 3 contact hrs/wk over 16 weeks). Immigration minimum: 12 credits UG, 9 credits GR per semester.', 'School of Medicine, Nursing, and Pharmacy are completely closed to exchange students; restrictions apply to Law, Nutrition, and Architecture courses (contact exchange@unm.edu).', '["Online home advisor nomination","Online UNM exchange application","Official transcript (>=3.0 GPA, certified English translation)","Proof of finances (<6 months old)","English proficiency proof (unless >=1 yr English-medium study exemption)","Passport biographical page copy","List of proposed UNM courses"]', '16-week semester US state research university (A-F grading rubric; transcripts issued 45-60 days post-term, $10 extra copies).', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Global Education Office / ISSS advising, check-in & orientation (>=1 wk prior), housing portals, and negotiated international student medical coverage.', 'Fall Semester: Partner Nomination Mar 15, Student Application Mar 31. Spring Semester: Partner Nomination Sep 15, Student Application Sep 30 (nomination links emailed Feb/Aug).', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/TUo New Mexico/UNM Information Sheet 2025-2026.pdf#page=5","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"16-week semester US state research university (A-F grading rubric; transcripts issued 45-60 days post-term, $10 extra copies)."},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:118","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"University-wide"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:118","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:118","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG","GR"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"Fall/Spring/Summer/Winter | Excel Col E also notes Winter term","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:118","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Fall","Spring","Summer"]},"campus_type":{"notes":"Main campus in Albuquerque, NM; campus_type label not explicitly classified in Fact Sheet.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/TUo New Mexico/UNM Information Sheet 2025-2026.pdf#page=6","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"partial","value":"US citizens cannot purchase UNM International Student Health Insurance (contact exchange@unm.edu)."},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:118","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Albuquerque"},"city_tier":{"notes":"Located in Albuquerque, New Mexico; city population figure not verified inside Fact Sheet.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"country":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:118","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"United States"},"course_catalog_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/TUo New Mexico/UNM Information Sheet 2025-2026.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"https://registrar.unm.edu/UNM%20Catalog/index.html"},"course_restrictions_note":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/TUo New Mexico/UNM Information Sheet 2025-2026.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"School of Medicine, Nursing, and Pharmacy are completely closed to exchange students; restrictions apply to Law, Nutrition, and Architecture courses (contact exchange@unm.edu)."},"credit_system_and_load":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/TUo New Mexico/UNM Information Sheet 2025-2026.pdf#page=5","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"US semester credits (3 cr = 3 contact hrs/wk over 16 weeks). Immigration minimum: 12 credits UG, 9 credits GR per semester."},"cross_references":[],"daily_life_english_friendliness":{"notes":"Not explicitly rated on unm.edu or Fact Sheet (US English-speaking campus).","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"eligible_auc_schools":{"notes":"Exact University-wide agreement scope.","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:118","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["ALL"]},"eligible_majors":{"notes":"Exact University-wide agreement scope.","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:118","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["ALL"]},"english_course_availability":{"notes":"US state flagship university teaching all regular programs in English.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/TUo New Mexico/UNM Information Sheet 2025-2026.pdf#page=4","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"full"},"english_course_list_url":{"notes":"All courses in https://registrar.unm.edu/UNM%20Catalog/index.html are taught in English; no separate English-only URL.","source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"english_proficiency_and_rhet1020":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/TUo New Mexico/UNM Information Sheet 2025-2026.pdf#page=3","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Exempt if attending a university where English is the medium of instruction for >=1 year full-time (applies to AUC) or qualifying HS diploma <=2 yrs old. Otherwise: UG TOEFL iBT 68 / IELTS 6.0 / PTE 47 / Duolingo 95 / C1-C2 169; GR iBT 79 / IELTS 6.5 / PTE 53 / Duolingo 105 / C1-C2 176; Law School TOEFL iBT 100."},"est_monthly_living_local":{"notes":"Derived monthly UG living budget from UNM 2026-27 academic-year Cost of Attendance divided by 10 months (2 semesters x 5 mo): Housing & Food $10,648-$12,471 + Books $1,869 + Transportation $2,498 + Misc/Personal $2,800 = $17,815-$19,638/AY ($8,907.50-$9,819/sem -> $1,781.50-$1,963.80/mo). Visa financial proof minimum is $7,500/sem ($15,000/AY) per Fact Sheet p.3.","source_ref":"https://bursar.unm.edu/tuition-and-fees/tuition-fee-information.html","source_type":"official_web","status":"partial","value":{"currency":"USD","max":1964,"min":1782}},"excel_rows":[118],"exchange_page_url":{"notes":"Incoming guide a