; final exams Apr 29–30, May 1 & 3, 2027 (2026-27 academic calendar).', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', 'USD', 1400, 1900, 8250, 'partial', 'UT Austin Student Health Insurance is mandatory for all J-1 exchange visitors and cannot be waived.', 'assisted', 'Housing options include on-campus UHD residence halls, UT apartments (such as East Campus Graduate Apartments), UT-managed off-campus apartments like 2400 Nueces, and private rentals/co-ops via Texas Global off-campus living resources.', NULL, NULL, 'Requires J-1 Exchange Visitor visa (Form DS-2019) issued after uploading financial proof in myIO: minimum $9,165 for 1 semester or $18,330 for 2 semesters.', 'http://www.utexas.edu/', 'https://global.utexas.edu/isss/students/exchange', 'http://www.registrar.utexas.edu/schedules', NULL, 'U.S. semester credit hours; reciprocal exchange students must maintain full-time enrollment: minimum 12 credit hours/semester for undergraduates (max 1 ESL course may count toward the 12-credit minimum), 10 for Law, and 9 for MBA.', 'Full-time course of study required; at most one ESL course through the English Language Center may count toward the mandatory 12-credit-hour undergraduate full-time load, and departmental course approval/prerequisites apply.', '["Digital academic transcript uploaded via myIO after admission","English proficiency verification (TOEFL iBT 79 / IELTS 6.5 or accepted equivalent)","Proof of financial support via myIO for Form DS-2019"]', 'Comprehensive U.S. public research university offering undergraduate areas of study across multiple colleges and schools with mandatory full-time semester enrollment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Texas Global / ISSS orientation, arrival check-in guidance, and International Hospitality Council (IHC) welcome and cultural programs.', 'Fall: nom window Jan 15–Feb 15 / app deadline Mar 1; Spring: nom window Jul 15–Aug 15 / app deadline Sep 1.', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://www.utexas.edu/academics/areas-of-