ing UAB Acceptance Letter). NIE printed on visa for stays up to 180 days; longer stays apply for TIE Student Residence Card post-arrival."}}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO universities (slug, excel_rows_json, shard, fact_sheet_match_status, fact_sheet_files_json, cross_references_json, official_name, short_name, country, state_or_province, city, region, agreement_status, agreement_student_levels_json, min_standing_note, agreement_scope_raw, eligible_auc_schools_json, eligible_majors_json, excluded_majors_json, min_gpa_host, instruction_languages_json, english_course_availability, english_proficiency_and_rhet1020, host_language_requirement, available_terms_json, fall_term_dates, spring_term_dates, final_semester_allowed, seat_quota, tuition_model, est_monthly_living_currency, est_monthly_living_min, est_monthly_living_max, living_cost_usd_est, living_cost_usd_est_status, mandatory_host_fees_and_insurance, housing_availability, housing_notes, host_grants_or_stipends, citizenship_restrictions, visa_lead_time_and_financial_proof, official_website_url, exchange_page_url, course_catalog_url, english_course_list_url, credit_system_and_load, course_restrictions_note, required_application_docs_json, academic_style, city_tier, campus_type, daily_life_english_friendliness, international_support_services, nomination_deadlines, ext_json, metadata_json) VALUES ('university-of-antwerp', '[128]', 7, 'matched', '["data/raw/factsheets/Antwerp/2024-2025/Exchange poster_FBE.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/Antwerp/2024-2025/UAntwerp - City Campus banner.jpg","data/raw/factsheets/Antwerp/2024-2025/UAntwerp FBE Factsheet Exchange 2025-2026.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/Antwerp/2026-2027/UAntwerp FBE Factsheet Exchange 2026.pdf","data/raw/factsheets/Antwerp/Exchange poster_FBE_2025.pdf"]', '[]', 'University of Antwerp', 'UAntwerp', 'Belgium', NULL, 'Antwerp', 'Europe', 'active', '["UG","GR"]', 'Bachelor-level (1... codes) courses require >=120 ECTS (2 completed years); Master-level (2... codes) courses require >=150 ECTS (5 completed semesters) prior to arrival.', 'Business Administration', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["English","Dutch"]', 'substantial', 'Good command of English (typically B2 CEFR level) required for English-taught FBE courses; RHET 1020 not mentioned.', 'None for English-taught FBE courses; proficiency in Dutch required only if taking Dutch-taught subjects.', '["Fall","Spring"]', 'AY 2026-2027 1st Semester (Fall): Exchange Orientation Day Sep 18, 2026; Classes start Sep 21-22, 2026; Christmas break Dec 19, 2026-Jan 3, 2027; Exams Jan 4-Jan 30, 2027 (mandatory in-person exam presence; Aug-Sep resits).', 'AY 2026-2027 2nd Semester (Spring): Begins early Feb 2027 (Feb 8, 2027); 13 weeks lectures + Easter break late Mar-mid Apr + 4-week June exam session (mandatory in-person exam presence; Aug-Sep resits).', NULL, NULL, 'auc_exchange_waiver', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'unknown', 'Tuition waived for exchange students; mandatory health insurance and Belgian municipal registration/residence permit fees apply. Overall Antwerp living costs estimated at €17,000-€18,000/year (~12-month cost-of-living guide).', 'assisted', 'University-affiliated residence rooms typically €360-€495/month (utilities included), or private Antwerp student market (UAntwerp Accommodation Team guides applicants; also in FBE Factsheet p. 3).', NULL, NULL, 'Non-EEA nationals staying >90 days must apply for a long-term student visa (Type D) at the Belgian embassy/consulate before traveling (do not enter on a tourist visa); UAntwerp issues an official invitation letter after Mobility-Online approval, and students must prove financial solvency (scholarship/grant, Annex 32, or UAntwerp blocked account). Residence permit required for stays >3 months (https://www.uantwerpen.be/en/study/international-mobility/erasmus-and-exchange-students/prepare-for-your-arrival/residence-permit/ and Factsheet p. 3). Exact lead time not stated.', 'https://www.uantwerpen.be/en/', 'https://www.uantwerpen.be/en/about-uantwerp/faculties/faculty-of-business-and-economics/studying-and-education/incoming-students/', 'https://www.uantwerpen.be/en/about-uantwerp/faculties/faculty-of-business-and-economics/studying-and-education/non-dutch-courses/', 'https://www.uantwerpen.be/en/about-uantwerp/faculties/faculty-of-business-and-economics/studying-and-education/non-dutch-courses/', 'ECTS credit system: recommended workload is 21-30 ECTS per semester (FBE offers >330 ECTS worth of English-taught exchange courses per Factsheet p. 2).', 'Master courses (2...) require >=150 ECTS (5 completed semesters); allowed up to 2 courses from other UAntwerp faculties under conditions. Mandatory in-person exam presence in Jan/Jun.', '["Home university nomination","Mobility-Online application","Transcript of Records (verifying >=120 ECTS for Bachelor / >=150 ECTS for Master)","English language proof (B2)","Passport / ID copy"]', 'Young, dynamic European business faculty (FBE at Prinsstraat 13 in Antwerp, a city home to +40,000 students) with mandatory in-person Jan/Jun exam sessions and Aug/Sep on-campus resits.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Mandatory Orientation Day, FBE buddy system + ESN Antwerp, and Housing / Visa / Residence Permit support teams.', NULL, '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":"Exam presence and retake policy detailed on p. 3.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Antwerp/2026-2027/UAntwerp FBE Factsheet Exchange 2026.pdf#page=1","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Young, dynamic European business faculty (FBE at Prinsstraat 13 in Antwerp, a city home to +40,000 students) with mandatory in-person Jan/Jun exam sessions and Aug/Sep on-campus resits."},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:128","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Business Administration"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:128","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"active"},"agreement_student_levels":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:128","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["UG","GR"]},"available_terms":{"notes":"Fall/Spring","source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:128","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":["Fall","Spring"]},"campus_type":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"citizenship_restrictions":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"city":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:128","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Antwerp"},"city_tier":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"country":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:128","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"Belgium"},"course_catalog_url":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"https://www.uantwerpen.be/en/about-uantwerp/faculties/faculty-of-business-and-economics/studying-and-education/non-dutch-courses/","source_type":"official_web","status":"verified","value":"https://www.uantwerpen.be/en/about-uantwerp/faculties/faculty-of-business-and-economics/studying-and-education/non-dutch-courses/"},"course_restrictions_note":{"notes":"Mandatory exam presence detailed on p. 3.","source_ref":"data/raw/factsheets/Antwerp/2026-2027/UAntwerp FBE Factsheet Exchange 2026.pdf#page=2","source_type":"fact_sheet","status":"verified","value":"Master courses (2...) require >=150 ECTS (5 completed semesters); allowed up to 2 courses from other UAntwerp faculties under conditions. Mandatory in-person exam presence in Jan/Jun."},"credit_system_and_load":{"notes":"330 ECTS catalog size verified in UAntwerp FBE Factsheet Exchange 2026.pdf#page=2.","source_ref":"https://www.uantwerpen.be/en/study/international-mobility/erasmus-and-exchange-students/application-documents/","source_type":"official_web",