 students MUST purchase W&J''s mandatory non-waivable CISI student health insurance plan (~USD 115/month, billed upfront for Fall/AY).', 'guaranteed', 'On-campus housing is guaranteed and required for exchange students (double room assignments with campus meal plan; residence/dining halls close over major winter breaks). 2026-27 standard double room USD 9,090/year + 19-meal board USD 6,516/year (https://www.washjeff.edu/total-cost-of-attendance/).', NULL, NULL, 'Requires US F-1/J-1 immigration form (I-20/DS-2019) backed by financial support proof covering any non-waived housing/meals/personal expenses and mandatory CISI health insurance (contact studyabroad@washjeff.edu).', 'http://www.washjeff.edu/', 'https://www.washjeff.edu/international-admission/', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["Exchange Student Admissions Application","1 recommendation letter from current professor","Financial Certification Form + notarized bank statement","Recent head-and-shoulders photograph","Short essay in English explaining reasons to study at W&J","Official English proficiency proof (TOEFL, IELTS, or Duolingo)","Copy of passport photo page","Official university-sealed academic transcript","Housing Preference Form","Copy of current academic schedule","Course Selection Form (4 preferred + 4 alternate courses)"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Free airport pick-up from Pittsburgh International Airport (PIT) on designated arrival days and on-campus free laundry (washjeff.edu; Office of Global Education studyabroad@washjeff.edu).', 'Fall / Academic Year: Nomination 1 March, Application 15 March. Spring / Calendar Year: Nomination 1 October, Application 15 October.', '{}', '{"academic_style":{"notes":null,"source_ref":null,"source_type":"unknown","status":"unknown","value":null},"agreement_scope_raw":{"notes":null,"source_ref":"data/raw/partner_list_extracted.json#Universities List!rows:157","source_type":"excel_list","status":"verified","value":"University-wide"},"agreement_status":{"notes":null,"sour